          "For WolPatcher, the repair stamps manifest.Version = the version detected before the repair while laying the fixed WolPayload snapshot. If the payload is older or newer than the installed version, can RecognizeFromManifestData mislabel the install? It depends on whether the payload's key-file MD5s match an UpdateInfo entry, which UpdateService.cs:1513-1518 says they never do.",
          "Does .NET 8 ZipArchive verify entry CRC32 on read? For unpinned GitHub assets, the direct path records hashes of the streamed bytes, so undetected entry corruption would be baked into FileHashes as 'canonical'.",
          "Have users actually hit (a) Uninstall leaving the clone after a Repair or full update (the ClonedAoe3 flip), (b) extra-copy shortcut hijack after a Repair, (c) addon originals lost after an intact repair? This would help prioritize.",
