        "area": "payload-sources",
        "summary": "WHERE REPAIR GETS ITS BYTES TODAY (all verified in code unless marked).\n\nEntry: RepairInstallAsync (MainWindow.xaml.cs:8006). A synchronous gate, CanResolvePayload (10396-10418), runs first. The actual lookup is deferred and memoized in EnsurePayloadAsync (8028-8029), which calls `ResolvePayloadUrlsAsync(overrideTag: targetReleaseTag)` (10319-10384). A plain repair passes null. Two sites consume it: the verify-first \"damaged\" branch (8212-8225) and the full re-overlay branch (8372-8387). Both call NativeInstallService.InstallModOnlyAsync (523-640). That method downloads the whole payload (DownloadAndConcatenatePartsAsync 875-993), then either extracts straight into the install (ExtractPayloadToDestinationAsync 1383-1549, used by WoL because DirectPayloadInstall=true, ModRegistry.cs:984) or stages it (ExtractPayloadAsync 1071-1170 plus CopyPayloadToDestinationAsync 1682-1797). Finally it rewrites the manifest (WriteManifest 2589-2659).\n\nSources by mechanism:\n(1) GitHubReleases. GitHubReleaseDownloader.ResolveAssetAsync (354-449):\n  - Tag: overrideTag, or else EffectiveGitHubTag. That is UpdateService.ResolveEffectiveGitHubTag (728-734), which returns the approved tag or the cached latest tag. It never returns the installed or pinned tag.\n  - External template: returns 1 URL with size -1 and a whole-file SHA-256. It refuses any tag other than the approved one (379-382) and refuses a missing SHA (384-395).\n  - Otherwise (GitHub-hosted): a complete .zip.001..N run from PickPayloadPartIndices (644-708), or a single asset from PickAssetIndex (566-614). Both exclude patch-* assets and userDataPayload. No SHA.\n(2) WolPatcher/other. UpdateService.EffectivePayloadZipUrls (175-182) returns the GLOBAL config override if set, else profile.Wol.PayloadZipUrls. The last resort is _config.InstallerZipUrl (MainWindow 10379). Pins travel only with the profile's own URL array (10370-10375). WoL's built-in payload is 3 parts of release 1.2.0e (ModRegistry 1000-1005). A catalog override is accepted only as https with one SHA per part (489-544).\n(3) DelegatedExternal/Manual: no payload. The Repair menu is disabled (13477-13484).\n(4) Only when a GH update or version pick has delta patches enabled and the target has no full zip: a baseline rescue via DeltaChainPlanner.BaselineUrlsOf (8309-8369).\n\nDownload mechanics (DownloadService 162-411):\n  - Per-part .part file plus Range resume, with a 416 branch.\n  - Retries: 4 attempts without progress, 12 total.\n  - Temp names are fixed (WolPayload.zip.NNN) in one shared TempDirectory.\n  - SHA is checked per part before concatenation (NativeInstallService 944-975).\n\nINSTALLED-VERSION QUESTION (verified latent bug): a plain repair of a GitHubReleases install always lays down and stamps EffectiveGitHubTag, never manifest.Version, LastKnownVersion or PinnedVersion. A \"Stay on this version\" or version-picked older install is therefore silently upgraded by Repair. The pin is left stale, because PinnedVersion is only touched when targetReleaseTag != null (8457-8464). This contradicts the UI promise \"Nothing is ever auto-updated\" (ModPropertiesDialog 461-481).\n\nRANGE-READ FEASIBILITY (verified live this session with curl, not with .NET):\n  - GitHub CDN: github.com answers 302 to a release-assets SAS URL, which answers 206. That held for the WoL part 3, Improvement Mod and K&B assets.\n  - WoL payload: 1,992,294,400 + 1,992,294,400 + 1,298,797,955 = 5,283,386,755 bytes. It is ONE single-disk Zip64 archive split by byte count:\n    - The EOCD cdOffset is 0xFFFFFFFF.\n    - 54,162 entries; the central directory is 5,361,984 bytes at logical offset 5,278,024,673, entirely inside part 3.\n    - The late entries carry a Zip64 local-header-offset extra field.\n    - The layout is flat (no wrapper folder), forward-slash names, deflate.\n  - Improvement Mod and K&B are classic (non-Zip64) zips.\n  - RemoteZipIndex (the only range reader in the repo) takes a single URL, refuses Zip64 (120-121), and parses only name, CRC and uncompressed size (147-158). It cannot locate an entry's data and cannot read WoL or any split payload.\n\nPath mapping: manifest keys are install-relative, forward-slash, compared case-insensitively. They equal `prefix + key`, where the prefix comes from ResolvePayloadPrefix (1294-1329) and must agree with NormalizePayloadRoot (1180-1211). That agreement is pinned by DirectPayloadInstallTests:170. bin\\ plays no part: FlattenBinSubfolder only touches clone files, which are engine files and not repairable.\n\nPer-entry integrity: the zip central directory's CRC32 comes from a remote that is not authenticated. The manifest's FileHashes (size + SHA-256) is the only trustworthy per-file anchor. It is NOT always equal to the payload bytes: it is re-captured for the PrivateSetupPath exe, addon-owned files, WoL-patched files and delta-hop files, and covered files are verified against the _originals snapshot.",
