        "invariants": [
          "Asset selection must go through GitHubReleaseDownloader.ResolveAssetAsync / PickPayloadPartIndices / PickAssetIndex. Never a second picker. These exclude patch-* assets and the declared userDataPayload (the data-loss bug class documented at GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:520-564) and require a gap-free 001..N part run ordered by part number (644-708).",
          "External hosting: only the approved tag is ever resolved and a SHA-256 is mandatory (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:379-395). ResolveEffectiveGitHubTag excludes external mods from follow-latest (UpdateService.cs:732). A range path must not create a route that bypasses either rule.",
          "Pinned SHA-256s cover WHOLE files (the external asset) or WHOLE parts (WoL catalog override, ModRegistry.cs:489-544). They are checked before concatenation or extraction (NativeInstallService.cs:944-975). Range-fetched bytes can never satisfy those pins, so every range-restored file must be proven against the local manifest's FileHashes (size + SHA-256). Anything unproven must fall back to the full, pinned download.",
          "Pins travel only with the profile's own URL array, never with a user-configured mirror (MainWindow.xaml.cs:10362-10376).",
          "Entry-to-install mapping must stay identical to the installer: GetFullPath(Combine(dest, entry.FullName)), zip-slip reject, forward slashes, case-insensitive keys, ResolvePayloadPrefix over file entries only (NativeInstallService.cs:1294-1329, 1406-1429). It must agree with NormalizePayloadRoot (1180-1211), which DirectPayloadInstallTests.cs:170 pins. Any new mapper must join that parity theory.",
          "FileHashes is not always payload-derived: the PrivateSetupPath exe (NativeInstallService.cs:2562-2575), addon-owned files (AddonService.cs:533-546), WoL patch-touched files (UpdateService.cs:1002-1007), delta-hop files (NativeInstallService.cs:731-740) and covered translation files (VerifyService.cs:108-117). A fetched entry that does not match the manifest must never be written or reported as repaired.",
          "A plain repair never applies delta patches (DeltaPatchService.cs:238-246, pinned by DeltaPatchTests.cs:113-133).",
          "Never thread the effective tag through targetReleaseTag/overrideTag (MainWindow.xaml.cs:10449-10452). A 'repair the installed version' tag needs its own parameter, or it triggers the version-pick auto-pin (8457-8464) and the 'version installed' bell (7979-7986).",
          "The repair tail order is load-bearing: ReapplyAddonsAfterOverlayAsync, then ApplyUserDataPayloadAsync, then stamp the version, then RaiseRepairFinishedBell, then the post-finally CheckAsync (MainWindow.xaml.cs:8414-8483, 8538-8592).",
          "The maintainer's model is 'reinstale todo junto con las actualizaciones': on damage, re-lay the whole overlay. Granular RepairFilesAsync was removed on purpose (git 8767ab2; CLAUDE.md:666-708). A per-file fast path is a policy change and needs explicit user approval, plus a guaranteed fallback to today's full path.",
          "A repair that does NOT re-lay the whole overlay must not rewrite the manifest's OverlayFiles/OverlayNetNew, run ApplyUpdateDeletions, or change Version (NativeInstallService.cs:592-613 applies deletions only on a GitHubReleases re-overlay).",
          "The direct path validates the downloaded zip BEFORE overwriting anything in a working install (NativeInstallService.cs:554-562). A range path must likewise stage and verify each file before it replaces the damaged one.",
          "Range readers must refuse a 200 (never buffer a multi-GB body), never throw into a version check, and degrade to the previous behaviour (RemoteZipIndex.cs:23-26, 166-187).",
          "Range reads must hit browser_download_url on the asset CDN, never api.github.com, to preserve the 60/h unauthenticated budget (CLAUDE.md:2408-2412; ResolveAssetAsync makes exactly one API call).",
          "The download retry and resume contract stays: .part + Range, the 416 branch, 4 attempts without progress / 12 total, and no retry on UnauthorizedAccess or user cancel (DownloadService.cs:112-207, 248-277; pinned by DownloadRetryTests)."
        ],
        "gaps": [
          {
            "problem": "A plain repair of a GitHubReleases install re-lays the EFFECTIVE tag (approved, or cached latest), not the installed tag. A user who pinned 'Stay on this version' or picked an older version is silently upgraded, and PinnedVersion is left stale.",
            "impact": "This breaks the UI promise 'Nothing is ever auto-updated'. It can break multiplayer parity with friends on the pinned version. The stale pin silently stops pausing future updates. Any range-read repair built on today's resolution would also fetch the wrong version's entries, which would all fail manifest-hash verification.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8028-8029, 10341-10343, 10454-10456, 8216, 8378, 8440-8445, 8457-8464; UpdateService.cs:728-734; ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:461-481"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The verify-first damaged branch cannot repair a delta-enabled mod whose effective tag is a patch-only release. The graph and rescue exist only in the else-branch, and ResolveDeltaTarget returns null for a plain repair.",
            "impact": "'Error: No asset matching ... in release X' leaks to the user and the repair silently aborts. This is the raw error that the rescue was written to eliminate.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8212-8213, 8246-8258, 8298-8309; DeltaPatchService.cs:241; GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:581-582, 441-444"
          },
          {
            "problem": "RemoteZipIndex cannot serve as a repair source. It refuses Zip64, takes a single URL (no split-part offset map) and discards method, compressed size, flags, local-header offset and Zip64 extras.",
            "impact": "It fails for WoL (verified Zip64, 5.28 GB, 3 parts) and for every split .zip.NNN GitHubReleases release. Even for classic zips it cannot locate entry data.",
            "evidence": "RemoteZipIndex.cs:104-128, 135-164, 62; live WoL EOCD bytes (cdOffset 0xFFFFFFFF, Zip64 extra on late entries)"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The only per-file integrity anchors are the local manifest's SHA-256 (not always equal to the payload bytes) and a remote, unauthenticated CRC32. Publisher pins cover whole files or parts only.",
            "impact": "Addon-owned files, the PrivateSetupPath exe, WoL files patched after the base, and files from patch-only delta releases cannot be proven from the base or target zip. They need transform-aware handling or a full-path fallback. Blind CRC-trust would weaken WoL and external-host security to 'whatever the host serves'.",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2562-2575; AddonService.cs:533-546; UpdateService.cs:1002-1007; NativeInstallService.cs:944-975; GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:405-406"
          },
          {
            "problem": "ModVersionFingerprint does not strip a wrapper prefix. Its candidates are chosen with PickAsset(r.Assets, null), which ignores AssetNamePattern and userDataPayload.",
            "impact": "A wrapped payload never matches (it degrades to null). A release whose small userdata.zip lands first can be indexed instead of the payload, also degrading to null. Version identification, which a range repair would use to find the installed tag of a detected install, is silently lost.",
            "evidence": "ModVersionFingerprint.cs:85-99; GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:182"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The global _config.PayloadZipUrls / InstallerZipUrl override applies to every non-GitHubReleases profile, not just WoL. The Verify panel's Retry reaches RepairInstallAsync without the menu's mechanism gate.",
            "impact": "A user-configured WoL mirror would be downloaded as the payload of a community WolPatcher mod (or of a DelegatedExternal/Manual mod reached via Verify retry). This contradicts 'generic for all mods'.",
            "evidence": "UpdateService.cs:175-182; MainWindow.xaml.cs:10367-10380, 10396-10418, 7702, 13481-13484"
          },
          {
            "problem": "PayloadResolution drops the resolved size and per-part sizes.",
            "impact": "A range path needs part boundaries to map logical zip offsets across .001/.002/.003. Today they are only re-learned via HEAD inside the downloader.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:10309, 10351-10352; NativeInstallService.cs:895-908"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The .part resume has no validator (If-Range/ETag), and temp part names are fixed and shared across mods and versions.",
            "impact": "If a repair is cancelled and another mod or version is then repaired in the same session, it can resume onto foreign bytes. Unpinned GitHubReleases payloads then fail late as a corrupt zip. The startup sweep only runs when the active mod is installed.",
            "evidence": "DownloadService.cs:292-298, 333-337; NativeInstallService.cs:108-109, 884, 917; MainWindow.xaml.cs:810-813"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The repair fallback's 'target has full zip' test uses PickAssetIndex only. BaselineUrlsOf omits nonPayloadAsset, and the planner ignores AssetNamePattern.",
            "impact": "A split-only target release takes the 'rescue' route with a misleading log and payloadSha256:null. Baseline selection can diverge from ResolveAssetAsync when a pattern is set.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8298-8307; DeltaChainPlanner.cs:192-208, 216-227; GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:425, 441"
          },
          {
            "problem": "A WolPatcher repair stamps manifest.Version = the detected pre-repair version while the bytes laid down are the base payload's.",
            "impact": "The manifest's Version and FileHashes/KeyFileHashes can disagree until the next post-patch re-stamp, which weakens 'manifest.Version names the bytes' as a repair source anchor. This matters only if the base ever differs from the installed version. Today both are 1.2.0e.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:10438-10439, 8216; UpdateService.cs:1019-1023"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The manifest stores no payload provenance: source URLs or tag per file, part sizes, ETag, wrapper prefix, or per-entry CRC.",
            "impact": "Repair has to re-derive which archive produced the on-disk bytes, and cannot pre-filter by CRC before downloading an entry.",
            "evidence": "Models/InstallManifest.cs:36-259; NativeInstallService.cs:2623-2648"
          }
        ],
        "opportunities": [
          {
            "idea": "A generic seekable HTTP range stream (Length, Seek, Read via single-range GETs, block cache of about 1 MB, 206-only, the 302-resolved SAS URL cached for the session) wrapped in a composite stream that maps logical offsets across ordered parts. Hand it to System.IO.Compression.ZipArchive in Read mode. The central directory and Zip64 parsing, entry naming/encoding, local-header skipping and inflation then come from the SAME reader the installer already uses (ZipFile.OpenRead, which reads the WoL Zip64 today). No hand-written zip parser.",
            "reusableCode": "ZipArchive/ZipArchiveEntry.Open (already used in NativeInstallService.cs:1398, 1485); per-part sizes from GitHub asset.size (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:429) or HEAD (DownloadService.TryGetRemoteSizeAsync 419-433); the 206-only discipline from RemoteZipIndex.GetRangeAsync 171-187; retry policy DownloadService.IsTransientDownloadFailure 112-147",
            "risks": "CanSeek must be true or ZipArchive buffers the whole stream. Reading the CD pulls all entries (5.4 MB and 54k entries for WoL, which is acceptable). The .NET redirect-plus-Range behaviour is unverified in code (curl only). GitHub/Azure support single ranges only, so non-adjacent damaged entries need one request each. The stream must not use AutomaticDecompression.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Covers a GitHub single asset (IM, K&B), GitHub split .zip.NNN (byte-split, EOCD in the last part), the WoL 3-part Zip64, the InstallerZipUrl/mirror, and external hosts that answer 206. Degrades to the full path when a host answers 200. Does not apply to DelegatedExternal/Manual (no payload) or to true multi-disk spanned zips, which the installer does not support either."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Per-file restore contract. For each damaged manifest key: map key -> entry (prefix + key). Pre-check the CD uncompressed size against FileHashes[key].Size. Fetch and inflate into staging while computing SHA-256 (and optionally CRC32 via System.IO.Hashing, already referenced). Replace the live file only when the SHA equals the manifest SHA. If ANY file can't be proven (no entry, size or SHA mismatch, transform-owned file, non-206 host, cost above a threshold), fall back to today's whole-overlay path unchanged. The manifest, deletions and version are not rewritten on the fast path.",
            "reusableCode": "VerifyService.ComputeFingerprintOf / ResolveHashTarget (VerifyService.cs:108-126); VerifyAgainstManifest output (138-218); the staging/replace discipline from DownloadService.ReplaceDestination (248-277); the AV-block handling in ExtractPayloadToDestinationAsync (1506-1512)",
            "risks": "This conflicts with the maintainer's deliberate removal of granular repair (git 8767ab2), so it must be approved and ideally opt-in or strictly fallback-guarded. Covered translation files need the live file and the _originals snapshot both restored, then the translation re-applied. Addon-owned files need the payload bytes restored and then ReapplyAllAsync. The PrivateSetupPath exe needs SetupPathPatcher run after the write, then comparison. A cost heuristic is needed (for example, sum of compressed sizes of damaged entries above X% of the payload means full).",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Security is the same for all mechanisms, because trust comes from the local manifest hash captured at a verified install and not from the host. That also covers the pinned WoL and external mods. Installs without FileHashes (old or detected, no manifest) cannot use it and keep the full path."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Extract the direct path's pass-1 planning (GetFullPath/zip-slip/relative/ResolvePayloadPrefix/dedupe) into one pure function returning key -> entryFullName, and use it in the installer, the range repair and ModVersionFingerprint. Fingerprinting then understands wrapped payloads, and mapping cannot drift.",
            "reusableCode": "NativeInstallService.cs:1406-1429 + ResolvePayloadPrefix 1294-1329; add a case to the DirectPayloadInstallTests.cs:170 parity theory",
            "risks": "Any change to the planning rule risks breaking healthy installs. Keep it a pure move, pinned by the existing parity tests before any behaviour change.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All zip payload shapes: flat, single or double wrapper, backslash names, duplicates, case differences."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Make repair source the INSTALLED version. For GitHubReleases, resolve the asset for manifest.Version, falling back to LastKnownVersion or PinnedVersion when it is a real tag of the repo, through a NEW parameter (not targetReleaseTag) that feeds EnsurePayloadAsync and the stamped version only. If the tag is gone, external-hosted and non-approved, or patch-only, fall back to today's effective-tag behaviour with an explicit notice. For patch-only installed tags, a later step could source files from the baseline zip plus patch zips, verified by descriptor sha256.",
            "reusableCode": "ResolveAssetAsync(settings, overrideTag) (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:354-449); ListReleaseGraphAsync + DeltaChainPlanner.FullZipOf (DeltaChainPlanner.cs:192-208); DeltaPatchDescriptor.Changed[].Sha256 (DeltaPatchService.cs:582-598)",
            "risks": "Policy question: should an UNPINNED install that is behind be brought to latest by repair (the WoL model) or kept on its version? Threading through targetReleaseTag would trigger the auto-pin and the bell. GitHubFollowLatestTests pins ResolveEffectiveGitHubTag, so leave that function untouched and add a separate one. Retagged or deleted releases 404.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All GitHubReleases mods (single, split, delta). Not WolPatcher, where repair is base payload plus the patch chain by design. Not DelegatedExternal/Manual."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Upgrade the version-identification half of RemoteZipIndex to the new range-stream + ZipArchive reader, or add a Zip64 locator/extra parser, plus multi-part support. Split and >4 GB GitHubReleases releases become fingerprintable, and pass the payload pattern/userDataPayload into ListReleaseCandidatesAsync.",
            "reusableCode": "RemoteZipIndex.TryLocateCentralDirectory/ParseCentralDirectory (tests in ModVersionFingerprintTests.cs); PickPayloadPartIndices (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:644-708)",
            "risks": "Must stay best-effort, never throw, and never block CheckAsync (UpdateService.cs:641-672). Extra range bytes per check (the CD is 5.4 MB for WoL-sized payloads versus about 250 KB today).",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All GitHubReleases mods. WoL keeps its UpdateInfo.xml MD5 detection."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Scope the global config payload override (PayloadZipUrls/InstallerZipUrl, and likewise UpdateInfoUrl) to the built-in WoL profile, and gate the Verify-retry repair entry by mechanism like the menu is.",
            "reusableCode": "UpdateService.EffectivePayloadZipUrls (175-182); the launcherCanInstall predicate (MainWindow.xaml.cs:13481-13483)",
            "risks": "A user who deliberately pointed a mirror at a community WolPatcher mod would lose that ability (a per-mod override would preserve it).",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Fixes every non-WoL WolPatcher, DelegatedExternal and Manual mod. No change for GitHubReleases."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Harden the resume path: send If-Range with the ETag/Last-Modified of the first response, or key temp part names by a hash of the URL, so a stale .part from another mod or version is never appended.",
            "reusableCode": "DownloadService.DownloadOnceAsync (284-411); NativeInstallService.DownloadAndConcatenatePartsAsync naming (917)",
            "risks": "Some hosts omit validators. Without one, keep today's behaviour. Changing temp names affects CleanupTempPayload/TryCleanupTemp sweeps (which delete the whole folder, so this is safe).",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Every mechanism that downloads a payload (WoL parts, GitHub assets, external, mirrors)."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Route the plain-repair damaged branch through the same graph/rescue logic when the effective (or installed) tag has no full zip, and use PickPayloadPartIndices as well as PickAssetIndex for the 'has full zip' test.",
            "reusableCode": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8264-8369 (graph + rescue); DeltaChainPlanner.FullZipOf (192-208)",
            "risks": "The rescue re-lays a baseline and patches upward. That violates 'plain repair never patches' unless the chain is pre-verified, so it needs a decision on whether repair may run fromSha256-verified patches.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Only delta-enabled GitHubReleases mods that publish patch-only or split-only releases."
          }
        ],
        "openQuestions": [
          "The maintainer removed granular repair on purpose ('reinstale todo junto con las actualizaciones', git 8767ab2). Is a range-read per-file fast path acceptable if every restored file is proven against the manifest SHA-256 and anything unproven falls back to today's whole-overlay path? Or should range reads stay diagnostic only (e.g. telling the user '3 files, 12 MB' before the full download)?",
          "Policy for GitHubReleases repair of an install that is NOT on the effective tag. (a) Pinned: fix repair to restore the pinned version? (b) Unpinned but behind with an update pending: keep 'repair brings you to latest' (current behaviour, consistent with the WoL model) or restore the installed version and leave the Update CTA?",
          "Which anchor is authoritative for 'installed version': manifest.Version (written together with FileHashes), ModState.LastKnownVersion (also set by fingerprinting of detected installs), or PinnedVersion? They can disagree (e.g. a WoL repair stamps the pre-repair version).",
          "Addon-owned damaged files: restore the payload bytes and rely on ReapplyAllAsync in the tail, or restore from addons\\_originals? Either way the manifest hash (addon bytes) cannot verify the fetched payload entry.",
          "Does .NET 8 HttpClient carry the Range header across the github.com -> release-assets 302 in this app's handler? Verified with curl only; CLAUDE.md:2411-2412 claims a manual .NET check.",
          "Does any live-catalog mod use externalAssetUrlTemplate, and does that host answer 206? The in-repo template has none.",
          "Does .NET 8 ZipArchiveEntry validate CRC32 on read? Not verified. It does not matter if SHA-256 against the manifest is mandatory.",
          "What cost threshold (count of damaged files, or compressed bytes as a share of payload size) should switch from per-file range reads to the full download, given that GitHub/Azure serve single ranges only?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "area": "engine-clone",
        "summary": "HOW THE BASE-GAME (CLONE) SIDE WORKS TODAY, all verified by reading the code unless marked otherwise.\n\nInstall (IsolatedFolder, NativeInstallService.InstallAsync, NativeInstallService.cs:165-368):\n- Phase 0 is a dry run of the clone (CountCloneableFiles, :195-204). The payload is then downloaded and extracted.\n- Before anything is written, the in-progress marker goes down, but only if the folder has no manifest yet (:245-247).\n- CloneAsync copies the source ROOT into the destination (:257). The source is `AoE3Detector.Installation.ModRoot`, i.e. the Steam root that contains bin\\ (MainWindow.xaml.cs:10693) or a root inferred by the dialog (InstallFolderDialog.xaml.cs:302, 603, 636).\n  - The copy overwrites with `FileMode.Create` (FolderCloneService.cs:347).\n  - Files matching the storefront `SkipPatterns` are skipped (:37-60), including `*-manifest.json`.\n  - Excluded subtrees are skipped (:261-329): the destination itself, sibling mod installs from `GetSiblingInstallPaths`, the fixed list `AlwaysExcludeTopLevelDirs` (\"Improvement Mod\", \"Wars of Liberty\", \"wol\", directx, msxml, translations), and any immediate subfolder that contains `*-manifest.json`.\n- Zero-file gate (:270-276). Then FlattenBinSubfolder (:280 / :1567-1647) copies `bin\\*` up to the root with `File.Copy(overwrite:false)`. If a file already exists at the root, the root copy wins. Then bin\\ is deleted.\n- The overlay baseline is captured (:285). The payload is overlaid, overwriting clone files (:294-298).\n- Cleanup: StripDeleteListArtifact (:308), RemoveSupersededCompiledXml (:313), RemoveCloneFilesRemovedByPatches (:314). Both clone-file removals are IsolatedFolder-only (:2129, :2190), use plain File.Delete with no backup (:2146, :2206), and are recorded only in DiagnosticLog.\n- ClassifyOverlay (:315). ApplyPrivateSetupPath (:320 / :2535-2578) patches `<install>\\<GameExecutable>` in place after the clone.\n- The marker is deleted (:332), then WriteManifest(clonedAoe3:true, aoe3SourcePath) is called (:334 / :2589-2659).\n\nWhat the manifest records (InstallManifest.cs, WriteManifest :2623-2648):\n- Files: the whole folder, re-enumerated on every manifest write (:2605, :2702-2729). It mixes clone files, overlay files, shortcut .ico, translations\\, addons\\ and anything else in the folder.\n- OverlayFiles: the payload paths.\n- OverlayNetNew: payload files that did not exist before the overlay. OverlayFiles minus OverlayNetNew is the set of clone files the overlay replaced (overlay wins).\n- FileHashes: size + SHA-256 for overlay files only.\n- EngineFileHashes: fingerprints for at most 7 curated EngineCandidates (VerifyService.cs:60-69) that exist and are NOT overlay-owned (ComputeEngineHashes :1865-1886). The overlay set used here is the FileHashes keys (:2642).\n- Aoe3SourcePath and ClonedAoe3.\n\nWhat it does NOT record:\n- a list of clone files, or fingerprints for them (other than the 7 engine files)\n- which source path a file came from (root or bin\\)\n- the exclusion set used at clone time\n- the files the pipeline removed\n\nMod-only / Repair / full Update (InstallModOnlyAsync :523-640):\n- No clone. The payload is overlaid again. ApplyUpdateDeletions runs for GitHubReleases, otherwise only the delete-list strip runs. The same two clone cleanups run (:610-611), then ApplyPrivateSetupPath (:618).\n- WriteManifest is called with `aoe3SourcePath: null, clonedAoe3: false` (:626-628) whatever the previous manifest said. Only the delta path keeps them (:794-797).\n\nRepair (MainWindow.RepairInstallAsync :8006+):\n- A plain repair checks only the overlay (VerifyAgainstManifest :8185). It never calls VerifyEngineFiles. The code comment at :8156-8157 says so.\n- If the overlay is intact, no re-overlay runs, so nothing is cleaned up (:8190-8197).\n- If anything is damaged, it calls InstallModOnlyAsync (:8214), which does run the cleanups and resets the clone flags.\n- Addons are re-applied in both branches (:8418).\n- The engine is verified only by the explicit \"Verify files\" action (:10246-10253), with the \"reinstall AoE3\" suffix. That action's Retry button starts RepairInstallAsync (:7702, :7770), which then reports \"nothing to repair\" for damage that is engine-only.\n\nDetection and sources:\n- ModInstallProbe.Inspect (:159-222) requires one of 4 engine DLLs at the root for IsolatedFolder (:190-193). For overlays it also accepts them in bin\\ (HasEngineNearby :110-111). It then checks the in-progress marker (:197) and manifest ownership (:218-219).\n- AoE3Detector.IsCleanAoE3Folder (:489-510) rejects a folder with a root install-manifest.json or any known mod marker. The fast path of FindAll (:37-183) does not apply that check.\n- GameLauncher.FindAoe3InstallRoot (:99-108) tries config.GameExecutable first (:153-161), then Aoe3ManualPath, then FindAll.\n- After install, nothing reads the source folder again. Aoe3SourcePath is only printed by InstallSnapshot.cs:108-109.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "claim": "Clone copies with overwrite (FileMode.Create); no hashes are computed during the clone copy",
            "evidence": "FolderCloneService.cs:336-379 (CopyFileWithProgressAsync, FileMode.Create at :347, no hasher)",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "FlattenBinSubfolder promotes bin\\* to root WITHOUT overwriting (root copy wins on collision), via File.Copy, then deletes bin\\",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:1586-1646 (File.Exists skip :1598-1607, File.Copy overwrite:false :1614, Directory.Delete :1637)",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "Therefore the source of any clone file at install-relative P is deterministically <src>\\P if it existed (and was not skipped/excluded), else <src>\\bin\\P",
            "evidence": "FolderCloneService.cs:160-161 (relative path preserved) + NativeInstallService.cs:1591-1598 (bin-relative -> root, root wins)",
            "verified": true
          },
