            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:582, 626-628, 2632-2633 (previous used only for UserData* :2621, 2644-2647); delta preserves at :794-797; callers MainWindow.xaml.cs:8214, 8347, 8376",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "UninstallService picks blanket delete versus overlay-only removal from ClonedAoe3. So after a damaged-branch Repair or a full update, uninstalling a clone deletes only OverlayNetNew and leaves the whole AoE3 clone on disk",
            "evidence": "UninstallService.cs:183-197, 347-348 (ShouldRemoveOverlayOnly = hasManifest ? (!clonedAoe3 || isRealAoe3Root) : isRealAoe3Root)",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "A plain Repair never checks engine files. An install broken only in its engine reads as intact, and the 'Verify files' Retry, which calls RepairInstallAsync, then reports 'nothing to repair'",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8170-8197 (VerifyAgainstManifest only), 8149-8157 comment; Verify: 10246-10253, 7702, 7770",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "RemoveSupersededCompiledXml and RemoveCloneFilesRemovedByPatches run at all three overlay sites (install, mod-only/repair, delta), are IsolatedFolder-only, delete with no backup, and are idempotent",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:313-314, 610-611, 780-781; guards :2129, :2190; File.Delete :2146, :2206; idempotence noted :2100-2102",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "CLAUDE.md says 'A Repair does NOT clean an install already made'. The code shows this is true only for the intact branch (the common case). A damaged-branch repair or a full-overlay update does run both cleanups through InstallModOnlyAsync. The WolPatcher update path (UpdateService.ApplyUpdatesAsync) never calls them",
            "evidence": "CLAUDE.md:615-616 (doc claim); code: MainWindow.xaml.cs:8190-8197 vs 8214 -> NativeInstallService.cs:610-611; grep shows no Remove* calls outside NativeInstallService",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "CloneFilesRemovedByPatches is set only on the WoL built-in (10 data\\*.xml.XMB). SupersedeCompiledXml is a catalog opt-in flag",
            "evidence": "ModRegistry.cs:960-966, 697; ModProfile.cs:611-637; InstallParityTests.cs:217-224",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "ApplyPrivateSetupPath patches the exe after the clone, is refused for non-IsolatedFolder, is idempotent (already-patched detection) and writes atomically (staging + File.Move). It re-captures the exe fingerprint ONLY if the exe is tracked in the overlay FileHashes",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2535-2578 (guard :2546, re-capture :2566-2576); SetupPathPatcher.cs:216-251",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "An exe that came from the clone and is later patched (the Struggle of Indonesia shape) is in neither FileHashes nor EngineFileHashes, because EngineCandidates has no exe. Verify cannot see damage to it, and copying it back from the source would undo the patch",
            "evidence": "VerifyService.cs:60-69; NativeInstallService.cs:2566-2576; SetupPathPatcher.cs:206-210 (doc says the exe comes from the clone for SoI)",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "The private key is derived from profile.DisplayName on every re-overlay. If DisplayName changes, Patch() finds neither the base key nor the new key and PatchExecutable throws, so Repair fails with StatusInstallSetupPathFailed",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2556; SetupPathPatcher.cs:221-232; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8518-8524",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "EngineFileHashes store the bytes in the INSTALL: taken at install/re-overlay time and refreshed after WoL patches and addon applies. They are not source fingerprints, but at install time they equal the source bytes for clone-owned files",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:1865-1886, 1898-1952; UpdateService.cs:1002-1007; AddonService.cs:540-545",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "ComputeEngineHashes hashes only files that are present, and WriteManifest runs after the cleanups. So a file the pipeline removed never enters EngineFileHashes",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:1881, ordering :313-336",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "The WolPatcher post-update manifest refresh updates FileHashes, EngineFileHashes, KeyFileHashes and Version, but NOT OverlayFiles or Files. Files that WoL patches add are not recorded as overlay/shipped",
            "evidence": "UpdateService.cs:990-1025",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "For IsolatedFolder, ModInstallProbe requires one of 4 engine DLLs at the ROOT. A single-install config whose cached path fails the probe has that path cleared, so an own clone that lost all 4 DLLs is forgotten and Repair cannot be reached",
            "evidence": "ModInstallProbe.cs:90-100, 190-193; UpdateService.cs:1111-1145, 1370-1379",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "The in-progress marker is written only by InstallAsync, and only when the destination has no manifest. InstallModOnlyAsync (Repair) never writes it",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:245-247, 829-846; ModInstallProbe.cs:137, 197",
            "verified": true
