          {
            "claim": "In an InPlaceOverlay repair, ApplyUpdateDeletions can delete ANY path under the install root through a payload delete.lst, which means the user's real game. It has no InstallType guard, and the backups are deleted on success",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:598-600, 1972-2015 (backup dir deleted :2010), 2236-2271",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "For InPlaceOverlay installs, OverlayFiles minus OverlayNetNew are base-game files that were overwritten with no backup, so the launcher has nothing to restore them from",
            "evidence": "InstallManifest.cs:125-137; NativeInstallService.cs:1805-1831 (ClassifyOverlay)",
            "verified": true
          },
          {
            "claim": "GetSiblingInstallPaths skips only IsStockGame. An InPlaceOverlay mod's install path is therefore passed as a clone exclusion, and BuildExcludedSubtrees also auto-excludes any immediate source subfolder that holds a *-manifest.json. Whether a real layout puts an in-place install at <source>\\bin (which would empty the engine out of the clone) is NOT verified",
            "evidence": "LauncherConfig.cs:1112-1135; FolderCloneService.cs:285-294; conflicting layout comments MainWindow.xaml.cs:10698-10701 vs ModRegistry.cs:1064-1066 vs GameLauncher.cs:118-135",
            "verified": false
          },
          {
            "claim": "An AoE3 clone plus mod install is about 11k files. This matters for sizing a per-file clone fingerprint record",
            "evidence": "UninstallService.cs:131 comment ('11,408 files'); from a code comment, not measured by me",
