          }
        ],
        "invariants": [
          "CloneAsync overwrites. The overlay must always be laid AFTER the clone and the flatten, and a repair must never re-clone into an existing install without re-laying the overlay afterwards (NativeInstallService.cs:290-293, 1373-1376; FolderCloneService.cs:347).",
          "Overlay wins. Source bytes must never be written over a path in OverlayFiles, including base-shadowing overlay files (OverlayFiles minus OverlayNetNew). ComputeEngineHashes already excludes overlay-owned keys (NativeInstallService.cs:1868-1879).",
          "The split between overlay and engine is hard. Engine or clone files never enter FileHashes and are never sent through the payload re-overlay (VerifyService.cs:30-33, 234-240; VerifyServiceTests.Engine_DamagedFlagged_AndNotInOverlayVerify).",
          "A missing clone file is NOT damage. The pipeline deletes clone files on purpose: CloneFilesRemovedByPatches, superseded .XMB, payload delete.lst, and WoL etc\\*_delete.lst. Only a recorded fingerprint may define a clone file as expected-present. Never use 'the source has it and the install doesn't' as a reason to copy (NativeInstallService.cs:1881, 1844-1855, 2124-2228; CLAUDE.md:590-619).",
          "Base-game files may be removed or rewritten ONLY in an IsolatedFolder (disposable clone). The InPlaceOverlay folder is the player's real game (guards at NativeInstallService.cs:2129, 2190, 2546).",
          "SelectCloneFilesToRemove never removes a file the payload shipped, and refuses rooted paths and '..' (NativeInstallService.cs:2167-2184; InstallParityTests.cs:193-213).",
          "SupersedeCompiledXml stays an explicit opt-in and must not become a derived rule: WoL keeps randomnames/unithelpstrings .XMB, and removing them causes OOS/version mismatch (NativeInstallService.cs:2104-2122; ModProfile.cs:611-627; InstallParityTests).",
          "The install stays byte-faithful to canonical peers. Never strip files that a canonical install keeps (RemoveStaleBuildArtifacts no-op, NativeInstallService.cs:394-404).",
          "privateSetupPath: patch only IsolatedFolder; the patch is idempotent and written through a staging file. Any file operation that can put the stock exe back must be followed by ApplyPrivateSetupPath and a re-capture of the exe fingerprint (NativeInstallService.cs:2535-2578, 615-618, 785-790; SetupPathPatcher.cs:206-251).",
          "Never copy from, or treat as a clone source, a folder that is a mod install: IsCleanAoE3Folder, and ModInstallProbe ownership via the manifest ModId (AoE3Detector.cs:489-510; ModInstallProbe.cs:199-243).",
          "The stock game (IsStockGame) is never excluded from a clone, never repaired, never uninstalled (LauncherConfig.cs:1119-1128; UninstallService.cs:113-119).",
          "WriteManifest enumerates the whole folder, so any scratch file or sidecar written inside the install must be deleted before WriteManifest, or be listed in VerifyService.IsLauncherArtifact (NativeInstallService.cs:330-336, 2702-2729; VerifyService.cs:312-324).",
          "Translation-covered files are verified against translations\\_originals, not the live file. Restoring a covered file must keep the snapshot and live file consistent, or re-apply the translation (VerifyService.cs:102-117, 260-261).",
          "Every operation that re-lays files must re-apply addons before it reports success (MainWindow.xaml.cs:8414-8418; .claude/rules/addons.md). Addon-owned files must not be silently reverted.",
          "WriteManifest must carry the user-data record forward (NativeInstallService.cs:2613-2647). The same carry-forward discipline should apply to Aoe3SourcePath and ClonedAoe3, which today it does not.",
          "Uninstall safety: blanket delete only when ClonedAoe3 is true AND the folder is not a detected AoE3 root. The drive-root, contains-AoE3 and foreign-manifest vetoes run first (UninstallService.cs:90-197, 347-348)."
        ],
        "gaps": [
          {
            "problem": "A full re-overlay (Repair damaged branch, baseline rescue, full update, version switch) resets ClonedAoe3 to false and Aoe3SourcePath to null for IsolatedFolder clones",
            "impact": "A later Uninstall does overlay-only removal and leaves the whole multi-GB AoE3 clone behind. Any future clone-repair also loses the recorded source. No test covers this",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:626-628, 2632-2633; UninstallService.cs:183-197, 347-348; delta keeps them only at :794-797"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Plain Repair never checks or repairs engine files, while the explicit Verify reports them and its Retry leads into Repair",
            "impact": "The user sees 'damaged' from Verify and then 'nothing to repair' from Repair. Engine damage can only be fixed by a full reinstall",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8149-8157, 8170-8197, 10246-10253, 7702, 7770"
          },
          {
            "problem": "No per-file record of clone files: no list, no fingerprints except at most 7 engine candidates, no record of root vs bin\\ origin, no exclusion set, no record of removed files",
            "impact": "Repair cannot tell 'damaged clone file' from 'file deliberately removed' or 'file owned by an addon or translation'. Only the curated engine files can be restored safely",
            "evidence": "InstallManifest.cs:97-188; NativeInstallService.cs:1865-1886, 2702-2729; removals only logged :2150-2153, :2217-2220"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The clone-sourced, patched exe used by privateSetupPath mods is not fingerprinted anywhere",
            "impact": "A corrupt or truncated game exe is invisible to Verify and cannot be repaired. Copying it back from the source without re-patching would make the mod load vanilla content",
            "evidence": "VerifyService.cs:60-69; NativeInstallService.cs:2566-2576; SetupPathPatcher.cs:206-210, 235-238"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Renaming the DisplayName of a privateSetupPath mod makes every later re-overlay throw SetupPathPatchException",
            "impact": "Repair and updates fail for that mod permanently until reinstall",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2556; SetupPathPatcher.cs:221-232; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8518-8524"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The retroactive clone cleanup (CloneFilesRemovedByPatches / SupersedeCompiledXml) only happens when a repair finds overlay damage, or on a GitHubReleases full/delta update. It never happens on an intact repair or a WolPatcher update",
            "impact": "Older WoL installs made from a 1.2.0e payload before the fix keep the 10 base-game .XMB (vanilla proto/techtree and the player's own language). Opted-in catalog mods keep superseded .XMB unless reinstalled",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8190-8197 vs NativeInstallService.cs:610-611; UpdateService.ApplyUpdatesAsync has no Remove* call; CLAUDE.md:615-616"
          },
          {
            "problem": "An own IsolatedFolder install that lost all 4 root engine DLLs is detected as EngineMissing and its cached path is cleared",
            "impact": "The launcher offers Install instead of Repair. The own manifest, which would prove ownership, is ignored",
            "evidence": "ModInstallProbe.cs:190-193; UpdateService.cs:1111-1145"
          },
          {
            "problem": "EngineCandidates are root-relative only, while HasEngineNearby also accepts bin\\",
            "impact": "For an InPlaceOverlay install whose DLLs live in bin\\, no engine fingerprints are captured at all",
            "evidence": "VerifyService.cs:60-69; NativeInstallService.cs:1880-1881; ModInstallProbe.cs:110-111"
          },
          {
            "problem": "In an InPlaceOverlay repair or update, a payload delete.lst can delete base-game files in the player's real AoE3, and the backup is discarded on success",
            "impact": "Permanent, unrecoverable edits to the user's game, which contradicts the 'never touch base files in place' policy used elsewhere",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:598-600, 1981-2010, 2236-2271 (no InstallType guard)"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The source AoE3 is never checked again after install. The fast path of FindAll does not check cleanliness, and FindAoe3InstallRoot trusts config.GameExecutable first",
            "impact": "Any naive re-copy from the source could bring in a different language, a patched AoE3, or another mod's in-place overlay (the stray age3n.exe class of incident)",
            "evidence": "AoE3Detector.cs:37-183 vs 489-510; GameLauncher.cs:99-108, 153-161; ModInstallProbe.cs:199-208"
          },
          {
            "problem": "For WolPatcher mods OverlayFiles is stale: files added by patches are not recorded",
            "impact": "A retroactive 'shipped set' built from manifest.OverlayFiles is incomplete for WoL, so a generic sweep could wrongly treat a patch-shipped file as a clone file",
            "evidence": "UpdateService.cs:990-1025"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Clone cleanups delete with no backup and no record",
            "impact": "A wrong catalog flag cannot be undone from inside the launcher, and after the fact the only evidence is DiagnosticLog",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2146, 2206"
          }
        ],
        "opportunities": [
          {
            "idea": "Keep the clone provenance across every re-overlay. In InstallModOnlyAsync, pass previousManifest.Aoe3SourcePath and ClonedAoe3 through to WriteManifest when profile.InstallType == IsolatedFolder and the previous manifest belongs to this mod. Force false for InPlaceOverlay. Add a unit test that a repair re-stamp keeps ClonedAoe3=true.",
            "reusableCode": "previousManifest is already loaded at NativeInstallService.cs:582; ModInstallProbe.ManifestClaimsAnotherMod (:272-293); the delta path already does this at :794-797",
            "risks": "Older builds stamped clonedAoe3:true on in-place overlays (UninstallService.cs:175-182). The InstallType gate plus the existing IsAoe3Root veto contain this. It cannot heal manifests that an earlier repair already reset (see open questions). It changes uninstall behaviour: a real clone is blanket-deleted again, which is what it should be.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Every IsolatedFolder mod (WoL, catalog clones) whose install came from InstallAsync. No effect on InPlaceOverlay (kept false on purpose), stock game, or DelegatedExternal/Manual (not installed by the launcher)."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Hash-proven engine restore inside Repair.\n- Plain repair also runs VerifyEngineFiles.\n- For each damaged or missing key, try every source root: manifest.Aoe3SourcePath, config.Aoe3ManualPath, then each AoE3Detector.FindAll ModRoot.\n- In each root, check <root>\\rel first, then <root>\\bin\\rel, which mirrors flatten's root-first rule.\n- Accept a candidate ONLY if its size + SHA-256 equals the recorded fingerprint. Copy it to a staging file, File.Move it into place, then re-fingerprint.\n- Skip covered (translation) files.\n- Reject any candidate path inside installPath.\n- If nothing matches, report 'reinstall/verify base game' instead of 'nothing to repair'.",
            "reusableCode": "VerifyService.VerifyEngineFiles/ComputeFingerprintOf (:120-126, :241-276); SetupPathPatcher staging-and-swap pattern (:239-249); MainWindow.EnsureInstallWritableOrElevate (:8205) and EnsureGameNotRunning (:8031); UninstallService.IsAoe3Root/ContainsAoe3Root (:375-398) as a write veto; AoE3Detector.FindAll/InstallationFromManualRoot",
            "risks": "Because only fingerprint-identical bytes are accepted, the file's origin path, source drift (language, patches), and a source containing another mod's overlay all stop mattering. Remaining risks:\n- The write may need elevation.\n- Engine hashes refreshed after WoL patches will not match the stock source, so the restore refuses. That is correct, but the user is still told to reinstall.\n- It must never run for InPlaceOverlay.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All IsolatedFolder clones with non-empty EngineFileHashes, whatever the mod or update mechanism. Not InPlaceOverlay (player's game: advise Steam/GOG verify instead), not the stock game, not manifest-less legacy installs (no fingerprints to prove against)."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Record clone fingerprints at install time so any clone file can be restored the same hash-proven way.\n- Compute SHA-256 while copying (IncrementalHash in CopyFileWithProgressAsync) and during flatten.\n- After the cleanups and the overlay, keep only files that survived and are not overlay-owned. Store them in a SIDECAR (for example install-root clone-fingerprints.json), not in install-manifest.json, because ModInstallProbe parses the manifest per folder.\n- Also record the removed set: the clone cleanups plus any delete.lst targets. That list is the explicit never-copy-back rule.\n- Build the restore selector as a pure function in the style of SelectCloneFilesToRemove: recorded minus OverlayFiles minus removed minus addon-owned minus covered minus launcher artifacts.",
            "reusableCode": "The hash-while-writing loop in ExtractPayloadToDestinationAsync (NativeInstallService.cs:1447-1504); PruneMissingHashes (:1844-1855); RecaptureHashes (:1898-1952) to refresh after patches and addons; AddonOwnership.Load (AddonOwnership.cs:43); VerifyService.IsLauncherArtifact (:312-324); InstallParityTests-style pure tests",
            "risks": "- Size: about 11k entries (roughly 1-2 MB of JSON).\n- The sidecar must be skipped by WriteManifest's enumeration and FindUnexpectedFiles, and must not use a '*-manifest.json' name (clone SkipPatterns and the auto-exclude heuristic look for it).\n- It goes stale if WolPatcher patches or addons change clone files without re-recording them.\n- Flatten uses File.Copy, so promoted files need their own hash pass.\n- Installs made before the change do not benefit.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Every IsolatedFolder install made after the change, for every mod and every update mechanism. Old installs fall back to the engine-only restore above. InPlaceOverlay excluded by policy."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Retroactive, idempotent clone cleanup inside a plain Repair's intact branch.\n- Build an OverlayCaptureResult from manifest.OverlayFiles and run the two existing removal routines.\n- Exclude AddonOwnership-owned paths.\n- Add an AoE3-root / drive-root veto, and IsolatedFolder only.\n- Back up to a scratch folder outside the install, or record the removed names; log them by name.\n- Show one status line saying what was cleaned and why.",
            "reusableCode": "RemoveSupersededCompiledXml / RemoveCloneFilesRemovedByPatches and the pure selectors SelectSupersededCompiledXml / SelectCloneFilesToRemove (NativeInstallService.cs:2065-2228); the OverlayCaptureResult record (:1677-1680); UninstallService.IsAoe3Root (:375)",
            "risks": "- For WolPatcher mods OverlayFiles misses files added by patches. For WoL the declared ten are measured as removed by the chain and not re-added (CLAUDE.md claim, not verified by me). A generic future WolPatcher mod would need the patch-touched set recorded first.\n- Two not-yet-healed peers who repair at different times will mismatch in multiplayer until both repair.\n- The current routines keep no backup; the file can be copied back from the source.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Only IsolatedFolder profiles that declare CloneFilesRemovedByPatches (WoL built-in) or SupersedeCompiledXml (catalog opt-in). A no-op for everything else, and a hard no-op for InPlaceOverlay (existing guards)."
          },
          {
            "idea": "privateSetupPath exe repair. Record the exe's post-patch fingerprint and its pre-patch source fingerprint, and the key already recorded as PrivateSetupPathKey. To restore: copy the hash-proven source exe, run ApplyPrivateSetupPath (idempotent), then re-fingerprint. For renames, treat 'contains the manifest's recorded PrivateSetupPathKey' as already patched, or re-patch old key to new key.",
            "reusableCode": "SetupPathPatcher.Patch/ContainsPrivateKey/PatchExecutable (:150-251); InstallManifest.PrivateSetupPathKey (:217-218); the restore mechanism above",
            "risks": "Patching the key changes the exe's Authenticode status and draws antivirus heuristics (already accepted). The rename path needs care: it re-points the registry key, and the old key must be removed by uninstall.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Only IsolatedFolder mods with privateSetupPath whose exe comes from the clone (the SoI shape). Mods whose payload ships the exe are already covered by the overlay re-lay."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Route an own IsolatedFolder install whose engine is missing into Repair instead of forgetting it. The trigger is Inspect == EngineMissing AND the manifest ModId is this mod (or PreviousIds) AND the path is not an AoE3 root. In that case keep the cached path and offer the engine restore.",
            "reusableCode": "ModInstallProbe.OwnerOf/ManifestClaimsAnotherMod (:272-303); UpdateService.ResolveInstallPath (:1111-1145)",
            "risks": "This changes detection, which feeds PLAY/Update. Only the repair offer may use this state: never PLAY, never adoption by the broad scan. A folder without a manifest must stay rejected.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Every IsolatedFolder mod installed by the launcher (they all have a manifest). Not InPlaceOverlay (HasEngineNearby, and the engine belongs to the user)."
          },
          {
            "idea": "InPlaceOverlay 'never touch' hardening.\n- In ApplyUpdateDeletions, when InstallType is InPlaceOverlay, limit explicit delete.lst targets to OverlayFiles (the mod's own), or keep the backups.\n- Keep repair for these installs strictly to overlay re-lay plus net-new deletion.\n- Engine damage there: tell the user to verify in Steam/GOG, never write.",
            "reusableCode": "NativeInstallService.ApplyUpdateDeletions/DeleteWithBackup (:1972-2271); ModInstallType checks already used at :2129/:2190/:2546",
            "risks": "A modder who relied on delete.lst to remove a base file in place would lose that ability. That matches the policy but is a behaviour change.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All InPlaceOverlay mods (current and future). No effect on IsolatedFolder."
          }
        ],
        "openQuestions": [
          "What is the real Steam on-disk layout (data\\ at the root vs inside bin\\)? Code comments disagree (MainWindow.xaml.cs:10698-10701 says overlays land in …\\bin; ModRegistry.cs:1064-1066 says data\\ is at the root). The answer decides whether an InPlaceOverlay manifest can sit inside a clone source's bin\\ (auto-excluded by FolderCloneService.cs:285-294 plus GetSiblingInstallPaths, which would give engine-less clones) and which fallback source path (root\\P or bin\\P) is hit first.",
          "How should installs whose ClonedAoe3 was already reset by a past repair be healed? Inferring it (IsolatedFolder + own manifest + engine at root + not an AoE3 root + Files much larger than OverlayFiles) re-arms a blanket uninstall. This needs a maintainer decision.",
          "Do WoL (WolPatcher) patches modify any EngineCandidate DLL? RecaptureHashes' comment says they may (NativeInstallService.cs:1917-1918). If so, a hash-proven restore from stock AoE3 will always refuse for those files on patched WoL installs.",
          "Is a sidecar of about 11k clone fingerprints acceptable in size and install time, and should it be refreshed after every WolPatcher patch and addon apply (RecaptureHashes touched set)?",
          "Should the retroactive .XMB cleanup be silent, or announced to the user? It changes what the game reads (language/proto) and the LAN .xmb version check between two not-yet-healed peers.",
          "Should repair EVER write hash-proven engine bytes into an InPlaceOverlay folder (the player's own game)? My recommendation is no: advise Steam/GOG verification.",
          "Unverified doc claim (CLAUDE.md:608-615): the 10 WoL .XMB are the only clone files a patched install lacks and no later patch re-adds them. The safety of a retroactive WoL sweep based on OverlayFiles rests on it."
        ]
