      {
        "area": "post-install-mutations",
        "summary": "WHAT THE MANIFEST MEANS TODAY. InstallManifest.FileHashes (Models/InstallManifest.cs:154-173) starts as the payload's bytes, captured during the overlay copy (NativeInstallService.cs:1725-1762 staged; 1437-1527 direct/WoL). After that, every mutation path overwrites the entry with whatever is on disk: the SetupPathPatcher re-capture (2566-2576), the WoL post-patch RecaptureHashes (UpdateService.cs:1002-1006), the addon RecaptureInto (AddonService.cs:533-546), and the delta patch, which recomputes from live bytes (NativeInstallService.cs:733-740). So FileHashes means \"the bytes expected on disk now\", not \"the bytes the payload holds\". Nothing records where a file's bytes came from. EngineFileHashes is re-captured from disk at every manifest write (2642, 1921, AddonService.cs:545, UpdateService.cs:1007). Covered (translated) files are hashed through the translations\\_originals\\ snapshot instead of the live file (VerifyService.cs:108-117, 179).\n\nWHAT CHANGES FILES INSIDE THE INSTALL AFTER THE FIRST INSTALL:\n(1) The PrivateSetupPath exe patch: in-place, IsolatedFolder only, idempotent. Runs on install, repair and delta, but not after WoL .tar.xz patches (2535-2578; SetupPathPatcher.cs:203-251).\n(2) Clone clean-ups that delete files: superseded .XMB and CloneFilesRemovedByPatches. Opt-in, IsolatedFolder only, re-run on every overlay (2065-2228).\n(3) delete.lst, net-new auto-deletion and PruneMissingHashes on GitHubReleases re-overlays and deltas (1972-2034, 598-604, 776).\n(4) WoL .tar.xz patches: overwrite and create files, apply delete lists (files and folders), leave etc\\*_delete.lst behind, and use upd_backup_<id> scratch inside the install (UpdateService.cs:863-924; ArchiveService.cs:47-156, 310-360). Afterwards: translation reconcile, then RecaptureHashes of touched∩OverlayFiles, then a KeyFileHashes+Version re-stamp, then addon re-apply (UpdateService.cs:951-1037).\n(5) GitHub delta hops: backup outside the install, post-verify, canonical restore of untouched covered files from the snapshot, deletions, a full WriteManifest re-stamp per hop, and a snapshot refresh (NativeInstallService.cs:652-810; MainWindow.xaml.cs:7809-7883). Translation reconcile and addon re-apply happen at the tail of RepairInstallAsync (8418, 8540-8564).\n(6) Translations: the pack is extracted into translations\\<id>\\. Apply copies the pack's listed paths over live files. The snapshot lives in translations\\_originals\\, keyed by file NAME. Revert copies the snapshot back (TranslationService.cs:76-297).\n(7) Addons: files written anywhere under the install. Backups go to addons\\_originals\\<id>\\, ownership to addons\\_owned.json. Fingerprints are re-captured only for addon files in OverlayFiles. ReapplyAllAsync runs after every repair (including intact ones), every delta chain and every WoL update (AddonService.cs:155-344; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8418; UpdateService.cs:1037).\n(8) The shortcut icon <id>-shortcut.ico in the install root. Recorded in manifest.Files, not in FileHashes (2401-2438; VerifyService.cs:319).\n(9) The install-in-progress marker: only during a fresh InstallAsync into a folder with no manifest, deleted before WriteManifest (236-247, 329-332, 829-846).\n(10) Hand-pasted or hand-edited files. They show up as corrupt, and the stale-snapshot fallback (UpdateService.cs:1453-1498) partially adapts.\nOutside the install: the user-data seed in My Games (copy-if-absent, carried forward by WriteManifest 2644-2647), the launch-time junctions (AoE3SetupPathRedirect/AoE3UserDataRedirect), and every game-written file the code knows about (My Games: Users3, Savegame, AI4, RM4, Age3Log.txt per the rules docs). No code proves or disproves that AoE3 writes into the install folder.\n\nHOW REPAIR WORKS TODAY. A plain repair verifies first. If anything is damaged, it re-lays the WHOLE overlay via InstallModOnlyAsync (MainWindow.xaml.cs:8170-8226; CLAUDE.md 666-716: granular repair was removed). That is why the post-hoc fix-ups exist. The patcher re-runs inside InstallModOnlyAsync, and addons are re-applied at the tail. Translations are reconciled only when asUpdate (8540). A plain repair therefore silently loses an active translation.\n\nWHAT A GRANULAR PAYLOAD RESTORE WOULD GET WRONG TODAY:\n- Addon-owned overlay files: the manifest expects addon bytes, so restoring payload bytes removes the addon for that file and fails the recheck.\n- The patched PrivateSetupPath exe: the unpatched exe comes back and fails the recheck.\n- WoL files a .tar.xz patch changed after the 1.2.0e payload: pre-patch bytes come back, the recheck fails and recognition drifts.\n- Covered files: verify hashes the snapshot, not the live file, so the payload would have to repair the SNAPSHOT, and a live copy would overwrite the translation.\n- Engine files: never restorable from the payload.\n\nWHAT MAY COME FROM THE PAYLOAD. Only paths that are in OverlayFiles, in FileHashes but not EngineFileHashes, not covered, not addon-owned, not the patched exe, and whose expected hash equals the payload entry's hash. That last condition cannot be evaluated from the manifest today without downloading and hashing the payload.",
