        "invariants": [
          "Overlay vs engine separation: files in EngineFileHashes are NEVER restored from the mod payload and are reported as 'reinstall the base game' (VerifyService.cs:30-33, 231-240; NativeInstallService.cs:1868-1879; CLAUDE.md 683-690). ComputeEngineHashes/RecaptureHashes never put a path in both maps.",
          "Covered files are verified against the translations\\_originals\\ snapshot, never the live file, so an applied translation never reads as corrupt (VerifyService.cs:22-29,108-117; pinned by VerifyServiceTests.cs:153 and :181). Any live-file check added must compare against the active pack, not against canonical bytes.",
          "The _originals snapshot must hold CANONICAL bytes at every RefreshOriginalsSnapshot call; version detection (UpdateService.cs:1403-1408), the MP fingerprint (Multiplayer/ModHashService.cs:135-156), KeyFileHashes re-stamp (UpdateService.cs:1530-1543) and revert-to-English all read it. Delta shows the required order: restore untouched covered files first, then WriteManifest, then refresh (NativeInstallService.cs:744-805).",
          "Manifest keys are install-relative FORWARD-slash paths; RecaptureHashes matches with Replace('\\\\','/') against OverlayFiles and a backslash silently fails to match (NativeInstallService.cs:1920; .claude/rules/addons.md 119-125).",
          "PruneMissingHashes after every deletion, or verify reports a false 'missing' and a repair resurrects an intentionally deleted file (NativeInstallService.cs:1833-1855, 2607-2611; UpdateService.cs:1006; AddonService.cs:270; CLAUDE.md 806-809).",
          "The post-patch order is load-bearing: translation reconcile/snapshot refresh BEFORE RecaptureHashes, and addon re-apply AFTER the hash refresh (UpdateService.cs:951-1037; CLAUDE.md 782-792).",
          "Addon re-apply is best-effort and never fails an update/repair, and it runs before the repair reports success (AddonService.cs:298-344; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8414-8418; addons.md 200-209).",
          "A re-laid addon file must get a FRESH backup of the newly laid bytes, never the previous version's (AddonServiceTests.cs:246-262; addons.md 185-191). The fix for the not-re-laid case must not regress this.",
          "Two addons may not own the same file (Conflict), and Blocked is never bypassed by allowMultiplayerRisk (AddonService.cs:182-202, 167-172; addons.md 169-174).",
          "WriteManifest must carry forward UserDataRoot/UserDataFiles/UserDataDirs/UserDataRootCreated (NativeInstallService.cs:2613-2647). Addon ownership lives in addons\\_owned.json, not the manifest.",
          "ApplyPrivateSetupPath is idempotent, IsolatedFolder-only, and must run after anything that can re-lay the exe, re-capturing its fingerprint (NativeInstallService.cs:2535-2578; SetupPathPatcher.cs:203-251).",
          "Superseded-XMB and CloneFilesRemovedByPatches removal are opt-in, IsolatedFolder-only and idempotent; an InPlaceOverlay install must never lose base files (NativeInstallService.cs:2091-2229).",
          "Byte-faithful install: the launcher strips nothing from the payload (RemoveStaleBuildArtifacts is a pinned no-op, NativeInstallService.cs:370-404).",
          "The in-progress marker is written only into a folder with no manifest and removed before WriteManifest (NativeInstallService.cs:236-247, 330-332).",
          "KeyFileHashes and Version are stamped together, computed the same way detection reads them (UpdateService.cs:1009-1023; CLAUDE.md 793-805).",
          "A plain repair never applies a delta patch (DeltaPatchService.cs:224-241). Delta hops commit the manifest and LastKnownVersion per hop (MainWindow.xaml.cs:7797-7805, 7866-7870).",
          "The user-data seed is copy-if-absent and never overwrites (UserDataPayloadService.cs:13-18).",
          "Every rule must be keyed off profile data (CoveredFiles, InstallType, PrivateSetupPath, UpdateMechanism, _owned.json), never a mod id. Adding a mod is a data change (multiplayer.md 'ADDING A MOD IS A DATA CHANGE')."
