        "gaps": [
          {
            "problem": "ReapplyAllAsync discards each addon's _originals backup and ownership record, then re-backs-up whatever is on disk. For every addon file the overlay or patch did NOT re-lay, the new 'original' is the addon's own bytes, and addon-added files gain a backup.",
            "impact": "After ANY repair (including an intact one), delta chain or WoL update, disabling an addon leaves its bytes in place and no longer deletes files it added. Re-capture then blesses the result, so verify stays clean and repair never restores the true original. The base file is lost permanently.",
            "evidence": "AddonService.cs:313, 323, 352-395, 502-526; triggered unconditionally at MainWindow.xaml.cs:8418 and UpdateService.cs:1037; AddonServiceTests.cs:246-262 covers only the re-laid case."
          },
          {
            "problem": "NSIS addons and addons whose archive is missing from AddonStore cannot be re-applied, and ReapplyAllAsync removes their backup and ownership BEFORE finding that out.",
            "impact": "The transparent-UI addon (heaven-1656) is silently lost or orphaned after every repair or update. EnabledAddons still lists it, the files cannot be disabled, and the originals are gone.",
            "evidence": "AddonService.cs:313-337; AddonRisk.cs:142-154 (installer-only zip → Empty); ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:2669-2689, 2802-2826; AddonStore.cs:51-56."
          },
          {
            "problem": "A plain repair that re-lays the overlay never re-applies the active translation, because ReconcileAfterUpdate runs only when asUpdate is set.",
            "impact": "The user's language silently reverts to English while the config and UI still say the pack is active. A WolPatcher install recovers only if pending patches trigger the auto-continue.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8540-8564 vs 8573-8591; NativeInstallService.cs:630-636."
          },
          {
            "problem": "RefreshOriginalsSnapshot copies live covered files unconditionally. Full re-overlays (install and repair) and the WoL post-patch reconcile run it while a covered file the operation did NOT rewrite may still hold translated (or addon) bytes. Only the delta path guards against this. WriteManifest's ComputeKeyFileHashes also reads stringtabley live.",
            "impact": "The snapshot gets poisoned, which breaks version detection, the multiplayer fingerprint (lobby rejection), verify (false 'corrupt') and revert-to-English. It triggers for any mod whose CoveredFiles are not all shipped in the payload, or when a .tar.xz patch omits a covered file while a pack is active.",
            "evidence": "TranslationService.cs:76-97, 378; NativeInstallService.cs:342-346, 630-636, 745-747 (assumption stated), 2669-2695; UpdateService.cs:956-960."
          },
          {
            "problem": "Verify never examines the LIVE covered file while a snapshot exists. Version detection and the MP fingerprint read the snapshot too.",
            "impact": "A damaged or truncated live stringtabley or unithelpstrings (the file the game actually reads) is invisible to Verify, Repair, detection and multiplayer. A granular repair that restores the payload's bytes onto the live file would instead wipe the translation, and it would not fix a damaged snapshot.",
            "evidence": "VerifyService.cs:108-117, 179-185; UpdateService.cs:1403-1408; ModHashService.cs:147-156; the pack's expected hash exists in TranslationPack.cs:32 (TranslatedHash) but is unused."
          },
          {
            "problem": "FileHashes conflates the expected on-disk bytes with the payload's bytes. Neither the payload-origin hash nor per-file provenance (payload, patch, addon, patcher) is recorded.",
            "impact": "A granular repair cannot tell whether restoring the payload's bytes is correct. Addon-owned files, the patched exe and WoL files changed after the payload would all be wrongly reverted, and each would fail the recheck. This is the core blocker for a smart repair.",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2566-2576, 1002-1006 (UpdateService), AddonService.cs:533-546, NativeInstallService.cs:733-740; DeltaPatchService.cs:538-545 already fails closed on exactly this mismatch."
          },
          {
            "problem": "WoL .tar.xz patches: created files are never fingerprinted, deleted files stay in OverlayFiles, and nothing records which patch last wrote a file.",
            "impact": "Patch-created files are unverifiable and unrepairable. A per-file repair cannot find the right source (a specific .tar.xz) for files a patch changed. Stale OverlayFiles entries feed later classification.",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:1943-1947; UpdateService.cs:878-881, 1002-1007."
          },
          {
            "problem": "The WolPatcher full repair lays the fixed payload version but stamps the manifest with CurrentVersion (the version detected before the repair). It also does not re-apply delete lists newer than the payload (ApplyUpdateDeletions is GitHubReleases-only).",
            "impact": "Latent, until WoL ships a patch newer than the 1.2.0e payload. Repair would revert patched files to 1.2.0e bytes, record the newer version, and recognition would trust it (baseline MD5s match), so no patches are queued and the install is stuck on the older content under the newer label.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8214-8225, 10425-10440; NativeInstallService.cs:598-604; UpdateService.cs:1586-1611; ModRegistry.cs:1000-1005."
          },
          {
            "problem": "EngineFileHashes is re-baselined from disk at every manifest write, addon apply/disable and post-patch refresh, not only for touched engine files.",
            "impact": "An engine file already damaged when a repair, update or addon toggle runs gets blessed, and 'reinstall the base game' can then never be reported for it.",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:2642, 1917-1921; AddonService.cs:545; UpdateService.cs:1007."
          },
          {
            "problem": "TranslationService.Apply writes every path the pack lists, not only CoveredFiles. The snapshot is keyed by file NAME only.",
            "impact": "A pack file outside CoveredFiles is flagged corrupt, reverted by repair and never restored by RevertToOriginal. Two covered files with the same name in different folders would share one snapshot slot. Future mods declaring CoveredFiles are exposed.",
            "evidence": "TranslationService.cs:233-259 vs 82-89, 281-294; VerifyService.cs:113."
          },
          {
            "problem": "RevertToEnglish ignores the profile's CoveredFiles and uses WoL's defaults.",
            "impact": "For any non-WoL mod with different CoveredFiles, revert restores the wrong files or none. The same default is used in UpdateService.cs:1406/1535, harmless there because stringtabley is the key file.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:14322; TranslationService.cs:33-54."
          },
          {
            "problem": "A PrivateSetupPath exe cloned from AoE3 is never verified. The .tar.xz update path never re-runs the patcher, and a damaged cloned exe makes ApplyPrivateSetupPath throw during repair.",
            "impact": "Repair fails with 'cannot patch the setup path' instead of saying 'reinstall the base game'. A PrivateSetupPath mod updated through .tar.xz patches could be left with an unpatched exe.",
            "evidence": "VerifyService.cs:60-69; SetupPathPatcher.cs:223-233; NativeInstallService.cs:2546-2560; UpdateService.cs:739-1045."
          },
          {
            "problem": "Addons can write covered files other than the 3 identity files. On the update-repair tail, addon re-apply runs before the translation reconcile.",
            "impact": "Addon bytes can end up in _originals, and a translation Apply or Revert silently overwrites addon-owned files. There is no conflict check between addons and translations.",
            "evidence": "AddonRisk.cs:91-96; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8418 vs 8548-8558; TranslationService.cs:252."
          },
          {
            "problem": "FindUnexpectedFiles does not recognise launcher bookkeeping under addons\\, the in-progress marker, or *.patching.",
            "impact": "The one diagnostic that could show what the game or users write into the install is polluted by the launcher's own files.",
            "evidence": "VerifyService.cs:311-324."
          }
        ],
        "opportunities": [
          {
            "idea": "Record where each file's bytes should come from. Add an immutable PayloadHashes map (or per-file provenance) to InstallManifest, written only by the paths that lay canonical content: the InstallAsync/InstallModOnlyAsync capture, and the delta hop (post-hashes of the new version). FileHashes stays 'expected on disk'. A file is restorable from the payload only when FileHashes[p] equals PayloadHashes[p] and the path is not owned by anything else. Old manifests without the map fall back to today's full re-overlay.",
            "reusableCode": "OverlayCaptureResult.Hashes (NativeInstallService.cs:1677-1680, 1725-1762, 1437-1527); WriteManifest fileHashes param + PruneMissingHashes (2589-2648, 1844-1855); delta hash merge (733-742); FileFingerprint (InstallManifest.cs:313-328).",
            "risks": "The map must be pruned on the same deletions as FileHashes, or a repair resurrects deleted files. WriteManifest rebuilds from scratch, so the new field must be handed in or carried like UserData*. Manifest size roughly doubles (thousands of entries; acceptable).",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Covers every mod shape (GitHubReleases full or delta, WolPatcher, catalog mods), with no mod ids. WolPatcher files changed by a patch correctly become 'not payload-restorable', which is safe but not yet granular for them."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Add a pure, unit-testable resolver that, for each damaged path from VerifyAgainstManifest, picks the correct source, in this order: engine file → 'reinstall base game' (never repaired); addon-owned (_owned.json) → re-extract that entry from the AddonStore archive or unpacked NSIS folder, then re-capture; covered file → rebuild the SNAPSHOT from the payload's canonical bytes, then copy snapshot→live or re-Apply the active pack; the PrivateSetupPath exe → restore from the payload, then ApplyPrivateSetupPath; FileHashes≠PayloadHashes (changed after the payload) → escalate to today's full re-overlay plus chain; otherwise → the payload entry. Only the payload bucket is written from the payload.",
            "reusableCode": "VerifyService.BuildCoveredSet/ResolveHashTarget/ComputeFingerprintOf; AddonOwnership.Load; AddonService ZipAddonSource/FolderAddonSource CopyTo (413-480) and RecaptureInto; TranslationService.Apply/RevertToOriginal/RefreshOriginalsSnapshot; NativeInstallService.ApplyPrivateSetupPath (make internal); ExtractPayloadToDestinationAsync per-entry streaming + zip-slip guard (1398-1427).",
            "risks": "Must keep the forward-slash key convention. The resolver must fail closed (escalate to full) when it doesn't know a path's owner. Any path it does not recognise must not be written. The recheck must be a HASH recheck of the repaired set only (cheap), unlike today's structural-only recheck.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Generic: every decision reads profile or manifest data (CoveredFiles, PrivateSetupPath, InstallType, _owned.json). It does not cover WolPatcher files changed by a patch; those escalate."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Make addon re-apply aware of what was actually re-laid. Pass it the set of files the operation re-laid (overlayCapture.AllFiles, touchedByPatches, delta touched). Only for those paths discard and re-take the backup; keep the old backup, and 'added' status, for files still holding the addon's bytes. Skip re-apply entirely when an intact repair re-laid nothing. Resolve the archive BEFORE touching the backup or the ownership record. For NSIS addons, resolve the unpacked folder and use ApplyFromFolderAsync, or store the NSIS output as a zip in AddonStore.",
            "reusableCode": "AddonService.ReapplyAllAsync/ApplyCoreAsync/CopyWithBackup/ApplyFromFolderAsync; the touched sets already computed in UpdateService.cs:768-881, NativeInstallService.cs:680-742, and capture.AllFiles in InstallModOnlyAsync.",
            "risks": "Must keep AddonServiceTests.Reapply_TakesFreshBackup_SoDisableCannotDowngrade passing, plus add the not-re-laid case. The touched set has to be threaded into MainWindow.RepairInstallAsync, since InstallModOnlyAsync currently returns nothing.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All mods, and the unmodded stock game: addons are mod-agnostic and work without a manifest."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Enforce one 'canonical before snapshot' helper on every re-lay path. Before an operation, if a pack is active, restore canonical bytes for the covered files the operation will NOT rewrite (the delta block, extracted into a helper). Or refresh the snapshot only for covered files in the touched set. Then run ReconcileAfterUpdate after every re-lay, plain repair included.",
            "reusableCode": "NativeInstallService.cs:754-771 (delta canonical-restore); TranslationService.ReconcileAfterUpdate; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8545-8564.",
            "risks": "Order relative to addon re-apply matters: a covered file owned by an addon needs an explicit rule, ideally refusing addons on CoveredFiles in AddonRisk, sourced from the profile. KeyFileHashes in WriteManifest must stay computed on canonical bytes.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Every mod that declares Translations.CoveredFiles, including covered files not shipped in its payload (the case that is broken today). No effect on mods without translations."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Extend verify for covered files. Keep the snapshot-versus-manifest check, and add live-versus-expected: expected is the pack's TranslatedHash (MD5, from the active pack's translation.json) when ActiveTranslationId is set, otherwise the snapshot's bytes. Report live damage as its own repair category, whose source is translations\\<id>\\ or the snapshot, not the payload.",
            "reusableCode": "TranslationService.GetInstalled/ListInstalled, TranslationPack.cs TranslationFile.TranslatedHash, HashService.ComputeMd5Async.",
            "risks": "Must keep VerifyServiceTests.cs:153 and :181 green (a translated live file is not corrupt; no snapshot means skip). The pack folder itself can be damaged, so fall back to re-downloading the pack or reverting to English.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Any mod with CoveredFiles. It is keyed by the per-mod covered list; WoL's defaults are not hard-coded."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Download less on repair where possible. For single-zip GitHubReleases payloads, extend RemoteZipIndex to also return local-header offsets and range-fetch only the damaged entries, checked by the central directory's CRC-32 and by SHA-256 against PayloadHashes. Where that is impossible (split WoL payloads, external hosts without range support), still download the full zip but WRITE only the damaged entries, which removes the clobbering either way.",
            "reusableCode": "RemoteZipIndex.TryReadAsync/GetRangeAsync (RemoteZipIndex.cs:61-80+); ExtractPayloadToDestinationAsync per-entry loop; ValidatePayloadZip; payload SHA pinning (payloadSha256).",
            "risks": "Range fetches must be hash-verified before writing. Zip64 and the multi-part format fall back to a full download. The GitHub API rate limit is not involved because this uses the asset CDN.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "The range-fetch half applies to GitHubReleases mods with a single .zip asset; WolPatcher's split payload and external hosts get only the write-less half. The write-only-damaged half applies to all mods."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Harden provenance and diagnostics on the WolPatcher mechanism. Record which patch last wrote each file (patch id per path) and fingerprint patch-created files into FileHashes/OverlayFiles as patch-owned, so a granular repair can re-extract just those entries from the CRC-verified .tar.xz (SharpCompress reader can skip entries). Stamp the repair's manifest Version with the version the payload actually contains, not CurrentVersion.",
            "reusableCode": "ArchiveService.ExtractTarXzWithBackupAsync (returns the touched set); UpdateService touchedByPatches; UpdateInfo DownloadInfo CRC32.",
            "risks": "The .tar.xz archives are solid-compressed, so extracting one entry still streams the whole archive (a download-size win only when cached). Changing the repair's version stamp interacts with recognition (RecognizeFromManifestData) and the auto-continue into pending patches, and needs tests.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "Only mods using ModUpdateMechanism.WolPatcher (today WoL), keyed on the mechanism, not the mod id."
          },
          {
            "idea": "Make the unexpected-files diagnostic trustworthy. Add addons\\, the in-progress marker and *.patching to IsLauncherArtifact, and log the extras at repair time too. That answers empirically, from real bundles, whether AoE3 writes anything into the install folder.",
            "reusableCode": "VerifyService.FindUnexpectedFiles/IsLauncherArtifact (290-324).",
            "risks": "Diagnostic only, so negligible; keep the output capped.",
            "appliesToAllMods": "All mods."
          }
        ],
        "openQuestions": [
          "Does AoE3, or any mod's exe, write files into the INSTALL folder at runtime (logs, caches, compiled .xmb, Startup\\*.con, crash dumps)? Code and docs only show My Games. The '[extra]' lines FindUnexpectedFiles writes to real diagnostic bundles would answer it.",
          "Does every catalog mod that declares Translations.CoveredFiles ship all of those files in its payload? If not, the full re-overlay snapshot poisoning (gap 4) is live today for that mod. Confirm that WolPayload.zip contains data\\unithelpstringsy.xml.",
          "Do WoL .tar.xz patches always include both covered files? If one is omitted while a pack is active, the WoL post-patch reconcile poisons _originals.",
          "Is a WoL patch newer than 1.2.0e expected? That decides whether the WolPatcher repair version-stamp problem (gap 8) is latent or imminent.",
          "Product decision: should a repair PRESERVE deliberate user hand-edits or hand-pasted patches (report them as 'modified' and leave them alone), or keep reverting them to the payload as today?",
          "Which PrivateSetupPath mods ship the exe in their payload versus take it from the AoE3 clone? (Code comments name Struggle of Indonesia as clone-sourced.) Is any PrivateSetupPath mod updated through the .tar.xz path?",
          "Should AddonRisk refuse addons that write any of the mod's CoveredFiles, not just the 3 identity files? This needs the profile passed to Assess, which is currently pure and profile-free.",
          "For GitHubReleases releases that ship patches only (the rescue path), no single payload's bytes equal the manifest. Should a granular repair of those files escalate to the baseline plus chain, or fetch entries from the baseline zip and re-apply only the delta entries that touch them?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "area": "mod-shapes",
        "summary": "MATRIX OF MOD SHAPES. Everything below was checked in code, in the live catalog cache (%LocalAppData%\\AoE3ModLauncher\\catalog-cache.json, fetched 2026-09-25, 6 manifests) and in the installed install-manifest.json files, all read-only, unless it is marked as coming from docs.\n\nHow a mod becomes a profile. Two mods are built-ins (ModRegistry.cs:893-1076). Every other mod comes from the catalog through ProjectToProfile (ModRegistry.cs:627-770). Built-ins win id collisions: the catalog can only add links and, for WoL, a SHA-pinned payload (ModRegistry.cs:368-380, 489-544). Some fields exist only on built-ins and are never projected from a catalog manifest: DirectPayloadInstall, CloneFilesRemovedByPatches, AntivirusFalsePositiveFile (ModRegistry.cs:657-701; ModProfile.cs:757-760). Wol.PayloadSha256 is projected for the WoL built-in only; a community WolPatcher mod loses it (ModRegistry.cs:703-712). install.payloadUrls and install.payloadSha256 are parsed (ModCatalogManifest.cs:305-317) but nothing reads them. An unknown mechanism falls back to Manual (ModRegistry.cs:878-889); an unknown install.type throws and the mod is skipped (871-876).\n\nDimensions:\n- InstallType: IsolatedFolder or InPlaceOverlay.\n- UpdateMechanism: WolPatcher, GitHubReleases, DelegatedExternal or Manual.\n- IsStockGame.\n- DirectPayloadInstall.\n- Split payload parts: WoL lists them in Wol.PayloadZipUrls; GitHubReleases finds .zip.001… at runtime (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:421-434).\n- External hosting plus SHA: approved tag only, no delta, no followLatest (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:374-407; UpdateService.cs:728-734; DeltaPatchService.cs:208-216).\n- deltaPatches, including patch-only releases.\n- followLatest.\n- privateSetupPath: IsolatedFolder only, adds an HKLM key and patches the exe.\n- setupPathRedirect (legacy): a junction at launch time only.\n- supersedeCompiledXml and CloneFilesRemovedByPatches: files deliberately removed from the clone, IsolatedFolder only.\n- userDataFolder, userDataPayload (writes outside the install, copy-if-absent) and userDataRedirect (a My Games junction at launch).\n- multiplayerProbeFiles.\n- translations (CoveredFiles checked against the _originals snapshot).\n- probe, marker and executable, and where the exe comes from: the payload or the AoE3 clone.\n- previousIds.\n- Install slot: the primary install or a labeled copy (ModState.OtherInstalls).\n\nREAL MODS:\n- **wol** (built-in)\n  - IsolatedFolder, WolPatcher (UpdateInfo https primary, http alt), not stock.\n  - DirectPayloadInstall=true.\n  - 3 split parts (WolPayload.zip.001-003 @1.2.0e), SHA-pinned through the catalog overlay (catalog has 3 payloadSha256).\n  - privateSetupPath, setupPathRedirect and supersedeCompiledXml all false. CloneFilesRemovedByPatches = 10 .XMB files.\n  - userDataFolder \"Wars of Liberty\"; no userDataPayload; no redirect.\n  - Multiplayer probe files: the default y files.\n  - Translations: repo papillo12/translations, folderRepo Gorgorito12/translations, covered data\\stringtabley.xml and data\\unithelpstringsy.xml.\n  - Probe data\\stringtabley.xml, marker art\\zulushield, exe age3y.exe (in the payload), AV false-positive file AI3\\wolai.upl.\n  - On this machine: 4 copies; the active one is \"Wars of Liberty (4)\" with ProductGuid \"{EB44…}_is1_Wars of Liberty (4)\", 54,162 hashed files, clonedAoe3=True.\n- **aoe3-tad** (built-in): InPlaceOverlay, Manual, IsStockGame=true, probe data\\protoy.xml, exe age3y.exe, no userDataFolder.\n- **improvement-mod** (catalog)\n  - IsolatedFolder, GitHubReleases, mandosrex/AoE3ImpMod_New, approved 19.07.2026, followLatest=true.\n  - No deltaPatches, no external hosting.\n  - Probe and exe age3m.exe with NO marker. That is the risky shape the docs warn about.\n  - No userDataFolder, no redirects, no privateSetupPath.\n  - Installed version is 06.09.2026, which is NEWER than the approved tag. 2,192 hashed files.\n- **knights-and-barbarians-remastered** (catalog)\n  - IsolatedFolder, GitHubReleases, Lyvione/…Knights-And-Barbarians, approved 1.3.6c, followLatest=true.\n  - previousIds [knights-and-barbarians]; installProductGuid knights-and-barbarians_launcher.\n  - userDataFolder \"Knights and Barbarians\"; userDataRedirect=true in the live catalog (the local template says false); userDataPayload userdata.zip.\n  - supersedeCompiledXml=true.\n  - Probe and exe age3k.exe; marker \"Knights and Barbarians\\RM3\".\n  - The installed manifest still says modId \"knights-and-barbarians\" (the old id) and records 1 seeded user-data file.\n- **napoleonic-era** (catalog)\n  - IsolatedFolder, GitHubReleases, papillo12/Napoleonic-Era, approved 2.1.7b, followLatest.\n  - privateSetupPath=true.\n  - multiplayerProbeFiles [data\\proton.xml, data\\techtreen.xml].\n  - userDataFolder \"Napoleonic Era Beta 2\".\n  - Probe and exe age3n.exe; marker data\\proton.xml.\n  - The exe IS in FileHashes; the manifest records privateSetupPathKey.\n- **struggle-of-indonesia** (catalog)\n  - IsolatedFolder, GitHubReleases, papillo12/Struggle-of-Indonesia, approved 1.2, followLatest.\n  - privateSetupPath=true, userDataRedirect=true, userDataFolder \"Struggle of Indonesia\".\n  - Probe data\\stringtabley.xml; marker art\\buildings\\soi.\n  - Exe age3y.exe comes from the CLONE. It is in neither FileHashes nor EngineFileHashes (checked on disk).\n- **kings-return**: deleted from the catalog (aoe3-mods-catalog commit 4468bea); the id is still in the user's userModIds.\n  - Last manifest: IsolatedFolder, GitHubReleases, followLatest, privateSetupPath, userDataRedirect.\n  - Multiplayer probes: protok, techtreek, stringtablek.\n  - exe age3k.exe — the same exe name as K&B.\n\nShapes no live mod uses: InPlaceOverlay (other than the stock game), DelegatedExternal, Manual (other than the stock game), community WolPatcher, deltaPatches, external hosting, setupPathRedirect, translations on a non-WoL mod.\n\nWHERE REPAIR IS OFFERED:\n- Gear menu (MainWindow.xaml.cs:13477-13484): enabled only for WolPatcher or GitHubReleases, when installed and not busy.\n- MenuRepairInstall_Click (9836-9848): refuses IsStockGame, but does not check the mechanism.\n- ModPropertiesDialog RepairBtn (ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:554, 567-572, 2086-2090): enabled for any installed mod and hidden only for the stock game. It goes through RaiseMenuClick, which ignores IsEnabled (MainWindow.xaml.cs:5364, 6574-6578).\n- The Verify Retry button calls RepairInstallAsync() directly (7702).\n- Inside RepairInstallAsync (8006-8593), the only gate is CanResolvePayload (10396-10418). For every mechanism other than GitHubReleases it trusts UpdateService.EffectivePayloadZipUrls, and that prefers the GLOBAL, WoL-named config override (UpdateService.cs:175-182; LauncherConfig.cs:1910-1930).\n\nREPAIR FLOW AS IT IS TODAY:\n1. A plain repair with FileHashes verifies first (8158-8198).\n2. If nothing is damaged it skips the download. If anything is damaged it re-lays the whole overlay through InstallModOnlyAsync, using the EFFECTIVE tag (10341-10343).\n3. Updates, version picks and manifests with no FileHashes go to the delta / baseline-rescue branch (8228-8390). A plain repair never uses patches (DeltaPatchService.ResolveDeltaTarget).\n4. The tail runs on every path, including an intact one: re-apply addons (8418), then the user-data seed (8423). Translation reconcile runs only for asUpdate (8540-8567).\n5. InstallModOnlyAsync (NativeInstallService.cs:523-640) then does, in order:\n   - ApplyUpdateDeletions, for GitHubReleases re-overlays only (598-604).\n   - Supersede and clone cleanup (610-611).\n   - Re-assert privateSetupPath (618).\n   - Create shortcuts, write registry entries and write the manifest, all with installLabel=null, clonedAoe3:false and aoe3SourcePath:null (623-628).",
        "facts": [
          {
