        "invariants": [
          "The stock game (aoe3-tad) is never repaired, verified or uninstalled. Keep the IsStockGame guard, and add it inside RepairInstallAsync as well, since today only its callers check it (MainWindow.xaml.cs:9841, ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:567-572, ModProfile.cs:686-690).",
          "An InPlaceOverlay install folder is the player's own AoE3. Never clone into it, never remove base files from it (supersede and clone-cleanup are guarded to IsolatedFolder), never patch its exe, and its manifest must keep clonedAoe3=false (NativeInstallService.cs:2127-2129, 2189-2190, 2546-2552; ModRegistry.cs:634-642; UninstallService.cs:183-197, 347-348; CLAUDE.md:990-999).",
          "An IsolatedFolder clone's manifest must keep clonedAoe3=true and its Aoe3SourcePath, because that flag is what lets uninstall do a blanket delete. The delta path already carries them forward (NativeInstallService.cs:795); the full path must too.",
          "A plain repair never applies patches; only an update or a user-picked version may (DeltaPatchService.ResolveDeltaTarget; CLAUDE.md:2504-2505).",
          "Payload SHA pins: the WoL payload is accepted only when every part comes with a 64-hex SHA. Pins apply only to the profile's own URLs, never to a mirror the user configured. An external asset needs its SHA and can only resolve the approved tag (ModRegistry.cs:520-544; MainWindow.xaml.cs:10362-10376; GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:374-407).",
          "Delta patch assets, and the declared userDataPayload asset, must never be picked as the full payload (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:425, 441, 509-540).",
          "Split payloads (.zip.001…) must be resolved as a complete contiguous set, or refused with the missing part named (GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:421-439; MODDING.md:1449-1452).",
          "Verify keeps overlay files and engine files strictly separate. Covered translation files are verified against translations\\_originals, never the live file (VerifyService.cs:30-33, 108-117, 241-276).",
          "privateSetupPath has to be re-asserted by every path that writes a manifest. The step is idempotent, re-captures the patched exe's fingerprint, and needs the elevation check EnsureInstallWritableOrElevate(installPath, profile) before any write (NativeInstallService.cs:615-618, 790, 2535-2578; MainWindow.xaml.cs:8205, 8235, 8629-8632).",
          "The user-data seed only adds missing files, never overwrites, and its record must be carried forward in every rewritten manifest (NativeInstallService.cs:2613-2647; UserDataPayloadService.cs:287-291; ModProfile.cs:603-607).",
          "GitHubReleases re-overlay deletions only touch net-new files from the previous manifest or delete.lst entries, with backups (NativeInstallService.cs:592-604; MODDING.md:704-735).",
          "supersedeCompiledXml and CloneFilesRemovedByPatches are declared by the mod, never inferred, and apply to IsolatedFolder only. A repair must not put back files these deliberately removed (ModProfile.cs:611-637; NativeInstallService.cs:2104-2129).",
          "Built-ins win id collisions. From the catalog a built-in only accepts links and a SHA-pinned WoL payload (ModRegistry.cs:368-380, 455-512).",
          "A manifest stamped with one of the mod's previousIds belongs to that mod. Any new repair ownership check must accept previous ids, or K&B, whose installed manifest says 'knights-and-barbarians', stops being repairable (ModInstallProbe.cs:272-293).",
          "Adding any field to ModCatalogManifest means bumping ModCatalogService.CacheSchemaVersion, which is 1 today (ModCatalogManifest.cs:24-31; ModCatalogService.cs:78).",
          "With DirectPayloadInstall, the payload zip is validated before anything is written over a working install (NativeInstallService.cs:554-562).",
          "Addons must be re-applied after a real re-overlay, before the success status is reported (MainWindow.xaml.cs:8414-8418; .claude/rules/addons.md).",
          "An unknown mechanism string degrades to Manual (listed but never auto-installed or repaired). An unknown install.type skips the mod (ModRegistry.cs:871-889)."
