            "impact": "Repairing a labeled copy (for example 'Wars of Liberty (4)') re-points the primary's desktop and Start Menu shortcuts and its Add/Remove entry at the copy. It also rewrites manifest.ProductGuid to the primary's GUID, so uninstalling the copy later deletes the primary's Add/Remove key.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8214-8225, 8347-8358, 8376-8387 (no installLabel); NativeInstallService.cs:623-628, 797, 2315-2328, 2349-2366; UninstallService.cs:752-754; the WoL (4) manifest's productGuid carries the label suffix"
          },
          {
            "problem": "A plain repair re-lays the EFFECTIVE tag instead of the installed version, and ignores PinnedVersion.",
            "impact": "Repair quietly changes the version. A pinned user gets moved off their pin. For a followLatest mod with an empty LastKnownLatestVersion, the effective tag becomes the approved tag, which can be older than what is installed (Improvement Mod: installed 06.09.2026 > approved 19.07.2026), so the repair is a downgrade. A version change can also break multiplayer matching.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:10341-10343, 10434-10437, 8440-8465; UpdateService.cs:728-734; launcher-config.json + catalog-cache.json"
          },
          {
            "problem": "When a plain repair finds damage and the target release ships only patches, it has no baseline-rescue fallback.",
            "impact": "Any future mod that uses deltaPatches with patch-only releases gets 'No asset matching…' when it tries to repair a damaged install, even though update and version-pick work.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8200-8226 (EnsurePayloadAsync only), 8255-8286 (graph only fetched when ResolveDeltaTarget != null), 8298-8369 (rescue in else-branch); GitHubReleaseDownloader.cs:441-444"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Some repair entry points ignore the mechanism check, and the payload fallback falls through to a global override named for WoL.",
            "impact": "The Mod Properties Repair button and the Verify Retry button reach RepairInstallAsync for DelegatedExternal and Manual mods. If the user ever set config.payloadZipUrls (a WoL mirror), the repair downloads WoL's payload, with no SHA pins, into that other mod's folder. Without the override the button is offered and then fails with DlgInstallNoUrlBody.",
            "evidence": "ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:554, 2086-2090; MainWindow.xaml.cs:5364, 6574-6578, 7702, 10396-10414; UpdateService.cs:175-182; LauncherConfig.cs:1910-1923"
          },
          {
            "problem": "An intact repair, and any re-overlay that leaves clone-owned files in place, still runs the addon re-apply. That deletes the addon's backups and backs up the addon's own bytes in their place.",
            "impact": "After one harmless 'Repair' on a healthy install, an enabled addon can no longer be removed: disabling it 'restores' the addon's bytes, and files the addon added get a backup instead of being deleted. This hits every mod, and it is worst for addons that overwrite stock clone files, which repair never re-lays.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8190-8197, 8418; AddonService.cs:285-344 (line 313 deletes backups), 381-388"
          },
          {
            "problem": "A plain repair that re-lays the overlay never reconciles or re-applies the active translation.",
            "impact": "A WoL player with a translation active ends up with English covered files while config and UI still show the translation as active. Any future mod that declares translations inherits the same problem.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8540-8567 (asUpdate only); NativeInstallService.cs:630-636; TranslationService.cs:373-413"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Repair never re-asserts the privateSetupPath state or checks the exe when it finds the install intact, and exes that come from the clone are not tracked at all.",
            "impact": "For SoI, NE and similar mods, a missing HKLM private key or an unpatched or damaged exe gets 'nothing to repair' and the game loads vanilla or fails. SoI's age3y.exe is in neither hash map.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8190-8197; NativeInstallService.cs:618, 2535-2578; SoI install-manifest.json engineFileHashes/fileHashes; CLAUDE.md:4397-4399, 4423-4426"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Repair never re-lays base clone files: engine DLLs, a stock exe that came from the clone, or cloned data.",
            "impact": "An install broken only in cloned files verifies as intact, or reports 'reinstall AoE3', and repair cannot fix it, even though the clone source is still recorded (until the first repair erases it, per the first gap above).",
