        "invariants": [
          "RepairInstallAsync is also the GitHubReleases UPDATE, version-pick and auto-continue engine (callers MainWindow.xaml.cs:7644, 10481, 11593, 11913). Any repair-specific change must be gated on plainRepair = !asUpdate && targetReleaseTag == null (8158).",
          "A plain repair must never take the delta path: DeltaPatchService.ResolveDeltaTarget returns null when !asUpdate (DeltaPatchService.cs:238-246; pinned by DeltaPatchTests.ResolveDeltaTarget_RefusesARepairAndPrefersThePickedVersion).",
          "The intact path must NOT return early. It falls through so the post-finally CheckAsync and pending-update continuation run (8190-8197, 8573-8591). The granular version broke exactly this (8767ab2 diff).",
          "The maintainer's product model is a repair that ends in a complete, known-good install and then chains pending updates ('reinstale todo junto con las actualizaciones', CLAUDE.md:697-722). A smarter repair must produce the same end state, including a rewritten manifest, not just fewer bytes.",
          "Elevation is prompted only when a write is about to happen, so an intact repair never shows UAC (8201-8205).",
          "Overlay and engine damage stay separate: engine files are never routed into the repair set and are reported with VerifyEngineSuffix (MainWindow.xaml.cs:10242-10253; VerifyService.cs:231-276; VerifyServiceTests.Engine_DamagedFlagged_AndNotInOverlayVerify).",
          "Covered (translatable) files are verified against the translations\\_originals snapshot, never the live file (VerifyService.ResolveHashTarget; VerifyServiceTests.CoveredFile_*).",
          "Any re-lay must re-apply enabled addons BEFORE reporting success (8414-8418; .claude/rules/addons.md), and the user-data seed must be re-checked (8420-8427). The bell must be raised BEFORE the post-operation CheckAsync (8479-8483).",
          "FileHashes must be pruned after any deletion, or Verify reports a false 'missing' and a repair resurrects stripped files (WriteManifest NativeInstallService.cs:2607-2611; VerifyServiceTests.PruneMissingHashes_DropsStrippedDeleteList_NoFalseMissing).",
          "The direct-payload path must validate the zip BEFORE overwriting a working install (NativeInstallService.cs:554-562; DirectPayloadInstallTests.ValidatePayloadZip_AcceptsAGoodZipAndRejectsGarbage). VerifyExtractIntact must stay a no-op on an intact payload (PayloadIntegrityTests, first test).",
          "Repair's progress UI must mirror InstallAsync's: phase weights DL 60 / Extract 20 / Overlay 20 (direct payload: 60/0/40), a phaseProgress that resets the SpeedTracker, and phase-aware speed keys (MainWindow.xaml.cs:8060-8147; CLAUDE.md:733-756).",
          "An InPlaceOverlay install must stay clonedAoe3:false, and only an IsolatedFolder clone may lose base-game files (CLAUDE.md:990-997; NativeInstallService.cs:2094-2098, 2129; UninstallSafetyTests; MultiInstallPhase1Tests). Any identity-preservation fix must carry forward the PREVIOUS manifest's flag, never force true.",
          "The stock game is never verified, repaired or uninstalled (MainWindow.xaml.cs:9841, 9853; ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:567-583; FilesAndAntivirusDialogTests.TheStockGameHidesEverythingThatCouldActOnIt).",
          "The launcher never edits antivirus configuration. The blocked-mode dialog cannot be silenced (AntivirusExclusionDialog.xaml.cs:26-31, 101-109; FilesAndAntivirusDialogTests.TheBlockedModeOffersNoWayToSilenceIt).",
          "Every new string needs both EN and ES and a unique key, and visible text must sit on named elements (StringKeyUniquenessTests, StringTableSourceTests, LocalizationGuardTests).",
          "The external-hosting SHA pin covers only the approved tag, and effective-tag resolution stays in UpdateService.ResolveEffectiveGitHubTag. Never thread the effective tag through targetReleaseTag, or the version pin triggers (UpdateService.cs:717-734; MainWindow.xaml.cs:10443-10456).",
          "Per user memory: never commit or push; the user handles git."
        ],
        "gaps": [
          {
            "problem": "The Verify-to-Repair handoff and all repair error text sit on a hidden panel. The Retry button (which runs the repair) and the DlgVerifyRepairBody explanation are never shown.",
            "impact": "After Verify finds damage, the user sees 'Operation failed' with no reason for 10 s, then a one-line list. They must find Repair on their own (gear > Properties > LOCAL FILES). Every repair error message (including the antivirus one) is also invisible until the status line takes over.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml:1596-1611; MainWindow.xaml.cs:4144-4206 (no mirror of ProgressMessageText/ProgressActionRetry), 7702, 7770, 9729-9754, 9696"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Verify and Repair disagree about what 'damaged' means. Verify counts structural, overlay and engine problems; Repair's pre-verify checks the overlay only.",
            "impact": "Engine-only or probe-only damage: Verify says 'N problems, repair?', then Repair says 'intact, nothing to repair' and fixes nothing. Engine damage is never repairable at all, and repair's manifest rewrite even re-blesses it.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:10112-10150, 10246-10253 vs 8185-8197; NativeInstallService.cs:2642, 1865-1886"
          },
          {
            "problem": "Antivirus loop: repair has no PayloadFileBlockedException handling and no preventive notice.",
            "impact": "A quarantined file makes Verify report it missing. Repair then downloads the full payload again, Defender deletes the file again, and the user gets a raw English exception on a hidden panel. Retry repeats the multi-GB download with no exclusion guidance.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8505-8530 vs 11411-11442 and 10852-10867; NativeInstallService.cs:887, 1056-1069, 1545; PayloadFileBlockedException.cs:24-25 ('A retry does not help')"
          },
          {
            "problem": "The full re-overlay does not preserve install identity: clonedAoe3 is set to false, aoe3SourcePath to null, and installLabel is dropped.",
            "impact": "After a repair (or a full-zip GitHub update), uninstalling a launcher-made clone removes only the net-new files and leaves the cloned AoE3 behind. Repairing a secondary copy repoints the canonical desktop shortcut and uninstall key at that copy. Aoe3SourcePath is lost, and any future 'repair engine files from AoE3' feature would need it.",
            "evidence": "NativeInstallService.cs:623-628 vs delta path 794-797; UninstallService.cs:183-197, 347-348; CreateShortcuts 2349-2355; TryWriteRegistryTo 2762-2763; MainWindow.xaml.cs:10890-10892"
          },
          {
            "problem": "A plain repair that re-lays the overlay drops the active translation from disk but leaves it marked active in config.",
            "impact": "A Spanish user who repairs gets English files while the UI still shows the translation as active. The multiplayer fingerprint and version detection are fine because they read _originals, but the user-facing state is inconsistent.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8540 (reconcile only when asUpdate); NativeInstallService.cs:630-636; TranslationService.cs:373-413"
          },
          {
            "problem": "For GitHubReleases, a plain repair silently switches to the effective (approved/latest) tag and ignores PinnedVersion. The verify step, meanwhile, compared against the installed version.",
            "impact": "A pinned user is upgraded by clicking Repair. The pin stays set but no longer matches the install. The bell says 'Repair complete' when it was really an update, and no translation compatibility reconcile runs.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:8212, 10341-10343, 10434-10437, 8457-8464, 8540; UpdateService.cs:728-734"
          },
          {
            "problem": "For WolPatcher, repair stamps the manifest with the detected version, not the payload snapshot's version.",
            "impact": "Latent. Once the base payload is older than the installed version, a repair lays old bytes but labels them with the newer version. If recognition then trusts the manifest baseline, the 'updates ride along' continuation would not fire. This depends on UpdateInfo MD5 behaviour, which is documented only in CLAUDE.md.",
            "evidence": "MainWindow.xaml.cs:10438-10439, 8216; UpdateService.cs:1513-1518, 1586-1599; CLAUDE.md:1919-1923, 771-773"
          },
          {
