    "critic": "# Completeness critique: mod repair redesign (read-only, plan mode)\n\nAll paths are relative to `C:\\Users\\Jeison\\Documents\\GitHub\\AoE3-Mod-Launcher\\WarsOfLibertyLauncher\\` unless stated otherwise.\n\nTags:\n- **VERIFIED**: I read the code in this session.\n- **DOC**: taken from CLAUDE.md only.\n- **PLAUSIBLE**: the code path exists, but I did not reproduce it.\n\n## A. Spot-check of the 5 most load-bearing claims (all confirmed)\n\n| # | Claim | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | A full re-overlay writes `clonedAoe3:false` and `aoe3SourcePath:null`. The delta path keeps both. | VERIFIED. `Services/NativeInstallService.cs:626-628` vs `:794-797`. Uninstall then takes the overlay-only branch (`Services/UninstallService.cs:183-197, 347-348`). That branch deletes only `OverlayNetNew` plus the manifest and never deletes a directory (`:647-687`). The multi-GB clone stays behind with no manifest. |\n| 2 | Addon re-apply runs even on an intact repair and deletes the backups first. | VERIFIED. `MainWindow.xaml.cs:8418` has no `intact` guard. `Services/AddonService.cs:313` deletes the backup and `:323` drops the ownership record, both before `resolveZip` at `:325`. `CopyWithBackup` then backs up the addon's own bytes (`:382-388`). The tests (`AddonServiceTests.cs:246-262, 346-361, 537-545`) only cover the re-laid case and an addon that was never applied. |\n| 3 | A plain repair of a GitHubReleases mod lays `EffectiveGitHubTag` and stamps `LastKnownVersion` even when intact. | VERIFIED. `MainWindow.xaml.cs:10341-10343, 10434-10437, 8440-8445`. For GitHubReleases, `CurrentVersion` is `LastKnownVersion` itself (`Services/UpdateService.cs:402-403, 491-493`); the manifest version is never read back. |\n| 4 | Repair never passes `installLabel`, and the manifest's identity is derived from that label. | VERIFIED. Calls at `MainWindow.xaml.cs:8214-8225, 8347-8358, 8376-8387`. Consequences: `ProductGuidFor`/`AppNameFor` (`NativeInstallService.cs:2315-2328, 2626-2627`), shortcuts (`:2349-2366`), registry (`:2762-2767`). On this machine the WoL copies really do carry suffixed GUIDs, e.g. `{EB448764-…}_is1_Wars of Liberty (4)`. |\n| 5 | Translations are reconciled only when `asUpdate`. | VERIFIED. `MainWindow.xaml.cs:8540`. Real config: the primary copy \"Wars of Liberty\" has `activeTranslationId: \"ES-LA\"` (`%LocalAppData%\\AoE3ModLauncher\\launcher-config.json`), so this bug would bite on this machine today. |\n\n## B. Corrections and contradictions between the maps\n\n1. **The mechanism gate on Repair does not exist in the visible UI.** One map lists \"Repair is enabled only for WolPatcher/GitHubReleases (13481-13484)\" as an invariant. That gate sits on `ActionPanelControl.MenuRepairInstall`, which lives inside `LegacyPlayContent Visibility=\"Collapsed\"` (`MainWindow.xaml:1601-1608`). The only visible entry point is Mod Properties. It is enabled for any installed mod (`ModPropertiesDialog.xaml.cs:554`) and fires through `RaiseMenuClick` → `RaiseEvent`, which ignores `IsEnabled` (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:5364, 6574-6578`). `MenuRepairInstall_Click` does not check the mechanism (`:9836-9848`). The other maps are right. **VERIFIED.**\n2. **\"Force `ClonedAoe3` false for InPlaceOverlay\" (engine-clone map) is wrong.**\n   - An extra copy of an InPlaceOverlay mod is a real clone: `overlayInPlace = InPlaceOverlay && !addNewSlot` (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:10682`). It then goes through `InstallAsync`, which writes `clonedAoe3:true` (`:11167-11204`; `NativeInstallService.cs:334`).\n   - The carry-forward must come from `previousManifest.ClonedAoe3`, not from `profile.InstallType`, with the `IsAoe3Root` veto as the backstop. The mod-shapes version (`previous?.ClonedAoe3 ?? false`) is the right one.\n   - Guards keyed on `InstallType` (`NativeInstallService.cs:2129, 2190, 2546`) treat such copies as in-place. That is conservative but acceptable.\n3. **The `installLabel` bug is not limited to Repair.** It also hits:\n   - every GitHubReleases update, version pick and baseline rescue of a copy (same `InstallModOnlyAsync` calls);\n   - the automatic continuation after a copy install (`:11489-11490` → `MaybeAutoContinueUpdateAfterInstall` → `RepairInstallAsync(asUpdate:true)` at `:11593`). This is latent: it only fires when `DeltaPatchService.IsEligible`.\n   - the delta path. It keeps the shortcuts but passes `installLabel: null` (`NativeInstallService.cs:797`), so the copy's manifest `ProductGuid`/`AppName` become the canonical ones. Uninstalling the copy afterwards deletes the primary's Add/Remove key (`UninstallService.cs:752-754`).\n\n   **New consequence for WoL:** the canonical key `{EB448764…}_is1` (`Path` / `Inno Setup: App Path`) is exactly what `RegistryService.FindInstallPath` reads (`Services/RegistryService.cs:14-39`). It is used as the detection fallback (`UpdateService.cs:1150-1158`), so after a repair the fallback can resolve to the copy. **VERIFIED.**\n4. **\"Updates ride along\" in the maintainer's model only holds for WolPatcher.** CLAUDE.md:717-722 (DOC) says an intact-but-behind install continues into its pending patches. For GitHubReleases, `_pendingDownloads` is always empty (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:11903-11905`), and the intact tail stamps the latest tag before `CheckAsync` runs. What actually happens:\n   - The Update button disappears, although the files are still the old version.\n   - `ReconcileUpdateFinishedNotification` (`:3147-3173`) sees the stamped version as an advance and raises a **false \"update finished\" notification**.\n   - The same stamp contradicts the copy rule at `:11291-11297` (\"do NOT stamp the copy… would hide a needed update\"). Copies registered through `RegisterInstall` start with no version (`Models/LauncherConfig.cs:476-487`).\n\n   The documented \"self-heal\" (CLAUDE.md:2444-2446) is about the Update button (`asUpdate:true`) on a detected install with no manifest. That case never takes the intact path, so fixing the stamp does not break it. **VERIFIED.**\n5. **Pause is broken beyond Repair.** `PauseButton_Click` (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:9409-9414`) never touches `NativeInstallService.Pause`, i.e. `_downloader.Pause` (`NativeInstallService.cs:84-92`). So the native download and the loop at `:1459` (`while (Pause…)`) never pause in `InstallAsync` either. Only the clone phase pauses. **VERIFIED.**\n6. **Process-name matching is verified, not just plausible.** The mod-shapes map rated it PLAUSIBLE. `EnsureGameNotRunning` uses `Process.GetProcessesByName(Path.GetFileNameWithoutExtension(GameExecutable))` with no path check (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:10041, 11882-11883`). The 4 WoL copies, Struggle of Indonesia (SoI) and the stock game (TAD) all run `age3y.exe`. Repairing one copy offers to kill a game running from another copy or another mod. **VERIFIED.**\n7. **The disk-space check is about 3.5× too low for WoL.**\n   - The repair allowance is a fixed `RepairAllowanceBytes = 3 GiB` (`Services/DiskSpaceService.cs:40`).\n   - The real peak in `%TEMP%` is the parts plus the combined zip before the parts are deleted (`NativeInstallService.cs:981-990`): about 2 × 5.28 GB ≈ 10.6 GB for WoL.\n   - Staged mods also add the extraction. **VERIFIED** (sizes come from the payload-sources map).\n8. **Not every item in a Verify result is a manifest key.** Verify mixes human-readable text into the list:\n   - `\"data\\protoy.xml (AoE3 base file — …)\"` (`:10148`)\n   - `\"art\\zulushield\\\"` (`:10171`)\n   - `\"data\\*.bar (no data archives found)\"` (`:10182`)\n   - engine entries with a suffix appended (`:10251`)\n\n   Any \"single verdict\" shared by Verify and Repair needs a typed result, not these lists. **VERIFIED.**\n\n## C. New facts from the uncovered areas\n\n**Multiple copies / OtherInstalls**\n- **The private registry key is per mod, not per install.**\n  - `PrivateKeyFor(profile.DisplayName)` (`Services/SetupPathPatcher.cs:112-137`; `NativeInstallService.cs:2556-2559`).\n  - Copies of Napoleonic Era or SoI share one HKLM key, and its `setuppath` belongs to whichever copy was installed or repaired last.\n  - Nothing re-points it at launch: `EnsurePrivateKey` is only called from `ApplyPrivateSetupPath`.\n  - Uninstalling any copy deletes the shared key (`UninstallService.cs:759-763`).\n  - `NeedsAdminForPrivateKey` (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:8675-8684`) will ask for UAC on every repair or update of the \"other\" copy.\n  - **Consequence:** re-asserting `ApplyPrivateSetupPath` on every repair (proposed by 3 maps) would make copies overwrite each other. **VERIFIED.**\n- **Per-install state vs per-mod state.** `LastKnownVersion`, `PinnedVersion` and `ActiveTranslation*` are per install (`LauncherConfig.cs:383-408`). `ActiveInstallLabel` is a label the user can rename (`:496-505`), so it cannot be the source of `installLabel`. The correct identity is the manifest's `ProductGuid`/`AppName`:\n  - a copy has `ProductGuid == EffectiveProductGuid + \"_\" + Sanitize(AppName)`;\n  - the primary has `ProductGuid == EffectiveProductGuid` (on disk, all 4 WoL copies follow this).\n\n  **VERIFIED.**\n\n**Uninstall interplay**\n- The folder left behind by an overlay-only uninstall of a repaired clone has no manifest. It is not excluded from future clones:\n  - `AlwaysExcludeTopLevelDirs` only names \"Improvement Mod\", \"Wars of Liberty\" and \"wol\" (`Services/FolderCloneService.cs:86-97`);\n  - the `*-manifest.json` heuristic finds nothing (`:285-294`);\n  - the config no longer lists it for `GetSiblingInstallPaths`.\n\n  So a leftover \"Napoleonic Era\", \"Struggle of Indonesia\", \"Knights and Barbarians\" or \"Wars of Liberty (N)\" can be copied into the next IsolatedFolder install cloned from the AoE3 root. **PLAUSIBLE** (code path verified, not reproduced).\n\n**Concurrency with the game running**\n- `EnsureGameNotRunning` runs only once, before the multi-minute verify (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:8031`), and is not repeated before writing (`:8205-8225`). Verify has no such check at all (`:7677-7706`). The game can be launched from a desktop shortcut or Steam in the meantime.\n- The writers open files with `FileMode.Create` + `FileShare.None` (`NativeInstallService.cs:1486-1487`). A locked file raises a sharing violation → generic catch (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:8525`) → half-written overlay with no rollback. **VERIFIED.**\n- `VerifyAgainstManifest` records any file it cannot read (a lock or an antivirus scan) as **corrupt** (`Services/VerifyService.cs:200-209`). A transient lock therefore triggers a multi-GB re-download. **VERIFIED.**\n\n**Background operations**\n- `_isBusy` is also true during a read-only check (`MainWindow.xaml.cs:13220-13221`). A Repair clicked from Properties during a background `CheckAsync` silently does nothing (`:9838, 8010`). **VERIFIED.**\n- Repair cannot run in the background. Only `InstallAsync` (`:10960`) and `ApplyAsync` (`:11671`) set `_operationIsBackgroundable`; Repair blocks mod switching (`:1696`) because it reads `_updateService` many times. If it becomes longer or backgroundable, it must capture `svc` the way `ApplyAsync` does (`:11678`). **VERIFIED.**\n- The notification sweep calls `svc.CheckAsync()` for other mods and saves the shared `_config` (`:13928-13965`), possibly while the repair tail is also saving it. **PLAUSIBLE**: a race on `launcher-config.json`.\n\n**UAC relaunch**\n- `EnsureInstallWritableOrElevate` relaunches with no arguments (`:8651`). The user has to click Repair again, and the verify runs again.\n- `--update-now` would not help GitHubReleases: it only calls `ApplyAsync` when `_pendingDownloads.Count > 0` (`:847-850`), which is always 0 for GitHubReleases.\n- `CanWriteTo` only probes the root folder (`Services/ElevationService.cs:41-57`). **VERIFIED.**\n\n**Repair while offline**\n- In the damaged branch, the order is: UAC (`:8205`), then the disk-space prompt (`:8207`), then `EnsurePayloadAsync` (`:8212`). Offline, resolving the asset throws; the code shows a raw \"Error:\" (`:10354-10358`) and returns quietly (`:8213`) with no `ShowProgressError`.\n- The user can go through UAC, a relaunch and another multi-minute verify only for it to fail. `ConnectivityState` is never consulted.\n- The intact path does work offline, and `AddonStore.ResolveAsync` is local-only (`Services/AddonStore.cs:51-56`). **VERIFIED.**\n\n**Installs with an unknown or detected version**\n- **WolPatcher:** `ResolveInstallVersion` = `CurrentVersion ?? LatestVersion ?? \"\"` (`:10438-10439`). With an unknown version and no network, the manifest's `Version` is written as \"\" and nothing is stamped (`:8444`).\n- **Detected WoL (Inno) install:** a repair overwrites the key `{EB448764…}_is1` with `UninstallString=\"\"` (`NativeInstallService.cs:2762-2776`). The original Inno uninstaller's entry is lost. **VERIFIED** (code); the impact is **PLAUSIBLE**.\n\n**Forward/backward compatibility**\n- There is no `[JsonExtensionData]` anywhere in the project. `WriteManifest` builds a new object each time (`NativeInstallService.cs:2623-2648`), and the WoL post-patch path does load + `Save` (`UpdateService.cs:992-1025`). An older launcher build therefore **silently drops** any new manifest (or config) field. Any new field (payload hashes, provenance, clone fingerprints) must be optional and recomputable, and its absence must mean \"unknown\". **VERIFIED.**\n\n**Invisible progress panel**\n- `ProgressPanelControl` sits inside the collapsed container (`MainWindow.xaml:1601-1608`). Any new outcome state (for example \"N damaged, you need internet\", \"engine damaged\", \"antivirus\") must reach the dashboard or a toast, or nobody will see it. **VERIFIED.**\n\n## D. Top risks any repair redesign must respect\n\n1. **Repair is not an isolated feature.** `RepairInstallAsync` also runs the GitHubReleases update, version pick, auto-continue and rescue (callers `:7644, 10481, 11593, 11913`). Gate every change on `plainRepair` (`:8158`), and extract a pure, tested planner before changing behaviour. Today nothing tests `RepairInstallAsync`, `InstallModOnlyAsync` or `WriteManifest`.\n2. **Install identity.** Carry forward `ClonedAoe3`, `Aoe3SourcePath`, `ProductGuid`, `AppName`, `Shortcuts`, `StartMenuFolder` and `PrivateSetupPathKey` from the previous manifest. Key this on the previous manifest, never on `InstallType`; keep the `IsAoe3Root` veto. It cannot heal manifests that were already reset. On this machine all 8 manifests still have `clonedAoe3=true`, so fixing this before anyone repairs avoids the damage.\n3. **Copies.** The label, the shared private key, the registry key that WoL detection reads, and the process-name kill are all shared between copies. Any \"re-assert X on every repair\" breaks the other copies until the key is per install or re-pointed at launch.\n4. **Never stamp a version that was not laid down.** On an intact repair, use `manifest.Version` or keep `LastKnownVersion`. Otherwise the Update button hides, a false notification fires, and the multiplayer fingerprint stops matching the UI. Honour `PinnedVersion`, and never pass the effective tag through `targetReleaseTag`.\n5. **Addons and translations.**\n   - Skip the addon re-apply when nothing was re-laid. Only re-back-up files that were actually re-laid. Resolve the archive before touching the backup.\n   - Reconcile translations after every re-lay, and do it **before** the addon re-apply, because `RefreshOriginalsSnapshot` copies whatever is on disk (`Services/TranslationService.cs:76-97, 378`).\n6. **Trust anchors.** Only a SHA-256 checked in this same run is trusted. `FileHashes` does not equal the payload bytes for the patched exe, addon files, patched files, delta-patched files, or files covered by a translation. Never write bytes that were not proven, and always keep a fallback to the full re-lay (the granular repair was removed in commit `8767ab2`; DOC: the maintainer's \"reinstale todo\" model, so a granular path needs their approval).\n7. **Transactionality.**\n   - Today files are written in place with `FileMode.Create`, the manifest is written last, and `Save` is not atomic.\n   - Any new path should stage the file, check its hash, then move it into place.\n   - Keep a journal outside the install folder. Do not reuse `InstallInProgressMarker`: it blocks the launcher from adopting the folder.\n8. **Engine/clone.**\n   - Never copy from the AoE3 source without hash proof (the source is re-validated only by name/`IsCleanAoE3Folder`).\n   - Never do it for InPlaceOverlay or the stock game.\n   - Never restore files that were removed on purpose (`CloneFilesRemovedByPatches`, superseded `.XMB`, `delete.lst`).\n9. **Concurrency.**\n   - Re-check the game right before writing, with a path-aware check.\n   - Tell \"unreadable\" apart from \"corrupt\".\n   - Snapshot `_updateService` if the operation gets longer.\n10. **Offline and elevation order.** Verify (works offline) → check connectivity and resolve the payload → only then UAC and disk space. Add a resume argument such as `--repair-now <modId>`.\n11. **Real disk-space requirement.** About 2× the payload in `%TEMP%` (direct install) plus the extraction for staged mods, using real sizes instead of 3 GiB.\n12. **Compatibility.** New manifest fields are optional and treated as \"unknown\" when missing. New catalog fields require bumping `CacheSchemaVersion`. Make every decision from profile data (`CoveredFiles`, `InstallType`, `PrivateSetupPath`, `UpdateMechanism`, `_owned.json`), never from a mod id.\n13. **Hidden panel.** Surface outcomes on the dashboard or in a toast, not on `ProgressPanelControl`.\n\nNo files were modified and no git commands were run."
  },
